V2_BODY_PURPOSES_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PURPOSES#] [#IABV2_LABEL_FEATURES#] [#IABV2_BODY_FEATURES_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_FEATURES#] [#IABV2_LABEL_PARTNERS#] [#IABV2_BODY_PARTNERS_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PARTNERS#] About Cookies are small text files that can be used by websites to make a user's experience more efficient. The law states that we can store cookies on your device if they are strictly necessary for the operation of this site. For all other types of cookies we need your permission. This website uses different types of cookies. Some cookies are placed by third party services that appear on our pages. You can at any time change or withdraw your consent from the cookie declaration on our website. Please state your consent ID and date when you contact us regarding your consent. For more information about the use of cookies at TU/e you can visit: https://www.tue.nl/en/storage/disclaimer Do not sell or share my personal information Deny Allow selection Customize Allow all Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact × search Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies University Teacher D... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies University Teacher Data Analytics and AI (Full-time or Part-time) Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Other academic staff Organisation: Department of Industrial Engineering & Innovation Sciences Apply no later than: 18-10-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 3.706 - € 6.682 Apply now Introduction Do you enjoy inspiring the next generation of professionals? Are you enthusiastic about data analytics and AI? We are looking for a university teacher to develop and teach courses on data analytics and AI, possibly next to a job, PhD, or Post-doc position they are already fulfilling. Job Description We are seeking a University Teacher to teach courses in data analytics and AI and to supervise student projects, including bachelor’s and master’s thesis projects. Teaching responsibilities include developing and continuously updating course materials based on the latest scientific advances. This is especially important in the rapidly evolving fields of data analytics and AI, because courses must incorporate up-to-date AI methods, tools, and techniques. At the same time, students need to develop the skills to use AI responsibly and effectively as part of their learning process. You will play a key role in equipping students with both a strong theoretical foundation and the practical competencies to do this. The position is based in the Information Systems group, in the Industrial Engineering and Innovation Sciences (IE&IS) department at Eindhoven University of Technology. You will be working with our professors, PhD students, and teaching assistants to deliver high-quality education. The Information Systems group develops methods, tools, and techniques that support the entire lifecycle of Information Systems development, including advanced analytics and AI. It focuses on leveraging data analytics and AI to enhance organizational decision-making. Applications across various sectors are studied, with a focus on healthcare, transportation and logistics, services, smart industry, mobility, and energy. As a member of the group, you will contribute to teaching students how to improve organizational decision making with data science and AI. In this role, you will be responsible for developing and delivering high-quality course materials, teaching lectures and tutorials, designing assignments and exams, and supervising student projects, including bachelor’s and master’s thesis projects. In addition, 20% of your time will be dedicated to education-related research. The position is initially offered for a period of six months on a full-time basis or up to twelve months on a part-time basis. The appointment can be combined with another part-time position, such as a role at another institution or an existing PhD or postdoctoral appointment at TU/e. Depending on performance and available funding, there may be opportunities to extend the appointment or move to a permanent position. This position offers a unique opportunity to contribute to the education of the next generation of data analytics and AI professionals, while helping shape the future of AI education at the university. Job Requirements The successful candidate will meet most of the following requirements: You have a Master's or PhD degree in Data Science, AI, Computer Science, Industrial Engineering, or a similar field of study. You possess strong programming skills, preferably in Python, and are comfortable applying them in data analytics and AI contexts. You have a strong interest in education and some prior teaching experience, for example as a teaching assistant. You enjoy collaborating in (teaching) teams. Your communication skills are excellent as is your proficiency in English and your ability to collaborate in an international setting. Experience with the Dutch or broader European higher education system is considered a strong advantage. The preferred starting date is January 1, 2027. A later date by up to 2 months is negotiable, but not preferred. Conditions of Employment A meaningful job in a dynamic and ambitious university, in an interdisciplinary setting and within an international network. You will work on a beautiful, green campus within walking distance of the central train station. In addition, we offer you: Salary in accordance with"
    },
    "https://www.tue.nl/en/working-at-tue/vacancy-overview/assistantassociate-professor-in-high-frequency-inp-electronics": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor In High-Frequency InP Electronics",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor In High-Frequency InP Electronics Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies Assistant/Associate ... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies Assistant/Associate Professor In High-Frequency InP Electronics Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Associate Professor Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 04-12-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 8.992 Apply now Are you excited to establish a pioneering research program in high-frequency InP electronics? Join us to develop next-generation compound semiconductor technologies that will define the future of ultra-fast communications, sensing, and computing systems. Introduction Applications like wireless communications and (radar) sensing are moving to increasingly high operating frequencies. Since chips are at their core, the semiconductor technologies need to scale to Terahertz frequencies. Here, the traditional silicon technologies start to break down. Indium phosphide (InP) electronics is not a new technology and is used in high-end applications. However, new developments in materials science, fabrication technology, and heterogeneous integration, coupled to a boost in anticipated future demand, creates a unique opportunity to build a globally visible research program at the intersection of advanced III-V semiconductor devices, heterogeneous integration, and next-generation electronic systems. Few locations worldwide offer such a combination of world-class academic expertise, advanced cleanroom infrastructure, semiconductor manufacturing capabilities, and direct access to leading industrial partners. Group You will join a highly international and collaborative research environment and be empowered to develop a distinctive and independent research identity in high-frequency electronics and semiconductor technology within the Photonic Integration (PhI) group in the Electrical Engineering department at Eindhoven University of Technology (TU/e). The group is already internationally recognized for photonic integrated circuits (PICs), with a strong track record in indium phosphide (InP) technology. This provides a comprehensive foundation for InP electronics. Recently we have developed in-house processes to leverage our 100 mm photonic integrated circuit prototyping line for InP transistors. Our research spans cleanroom process development, component design, and application-specific integrated circuits. The group plays a key role in European Chips Act projects and pilot lines, and is now leveraging synergies between III-V photonics and high-performance III-V electronics, in close collaboration with our Integrated Circuits group. Our work is supported by TU/e’s state-of-the-art Nanolab cleanroom facility, specializing in III-V processing, and benefits from strong collaborations with other Electrical Engineering research groups and the local high-tech ecosystem. Job Description As an Assistant/Associate Professor, you will: Develop an independent research line in innovative electronic device technologies that can push the frontiers of advanced electronics for high-performance circuits, with potential applications in data centers, AI acceleration, 6G, radar, and sensor technologies. Explore areas such as high-speed III-V component design, semiconductor epitaxial engineering, and fabrication of active components (e.g., diodes, HEMTs, HBTs), thereby leveraging our existing research infrastructure, like our cleanroom infrastructure and process knowledge. Contribute to TU/e’s educational mission by teaching BSc and MSc courses, supervise PhD students and postdocs, and potentially contribute to life-long learning activities. Actively pursue research funding through national and European programs (e.g., Dutch subsidy, Horizon Europe, European Research Council, Chips Joint Undertaking) and industry collaborations. In this role, you will contribute to the ambition of the Beethoven program to educate top talent and strengthen research across the fields of Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics (STEM). Job Requirements The ideal candidate: Holds a PhD in Electrical Engineering, Applied Physics, or a closely related field. Has expertise in one or more of the following: High-speed III-V component design at the process level, semiconductor epitaxial engineering and/or fabrication of active components such as diodes and transistors (HEMT, HBT). Demonstrates strong research potential and ability to operate in a multidisciplinary environment. Shows affinity with teaching and will commit to obtaining the University Teaching Qualification. Has motivation to secure research funding and build collaborations with industry and academia. Possesses excellent communication and organizational skills and the ability to motivate researchers. Conditions of Employment A meaningful job in a dynamic and ambitious university, in an interdisciplinary setting and within an international network. You will work on a beautiful, green campus within walking distance of the central train station. In addition, we offer you: Salary in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities , scale 11 - 14, min. € 4,925 max. € 8,992 gross per month (on a full-time basis). In addition to your base salary, you will receive an 8% holiday allowance and an 8.3% year-end bonus, both calculated based on your annual gross base salary. Generous leave options: a standard 29 days (based on a 38 hour working week) per year that you can increase to 41 days by working two hours more per week (flexible working hours). This is prorated if you work part-time. As a TU/e employee, you participate in the ABP pension scheme, providing retirement pension and pension benefits for surviving dependents and occupational disability. TU/e pays 70% of the pension premium, while employees contribute the remaining 30%. A dedicated mentoring program to help you get to know the university and the Dutch (research) environment. A Development Track with the prospect of becoming an Associate Professor. If you have a more senior profile, a tailor-made career proposal will be considered. High-quality training programs for academic leadership and teaching. An excellent technical infrastructure, on-campus children's day care. Unlimited access to the modern on‑campus TU/e Student Sports Center at a very affordable rate. We support your wellbeing with free 24/7 access to OpenUp, providing you and your family with mental health support, expert guidance, and online training. Partially paid parental leave and an allowance for commuting, working from home and internet costs. A Staff Immigration Team is available for international candidates , as are a tax compensation scheme (the Expat Scheme ) and partner career support . On our website you can discover even more information about our conditions of employment . Build your career at TU/e! About us We are a leading international university where scientific curiosity meets a hands-on mindset. We work in an open and collaborative way with high-tech industries to tackle complex societal challenges. Our responsible and respectful approach ensures impact — today and in the future. TU/e is home to over 13,000 students and more than 7,000 staff, forming a diverse and vibrant academic community. Discover what Light Up means to TU/e in our short company video . Our university is located in Brainport Eindhoven — a world‑leading tech region with more than 7,000 high‑tech companies and strong R&D activity. Known for breakthroughs in AI, photonics, semiconductors and advanced manufacturing, Brainport is a place where technology serves people and society. Learn more about the Brainport region here . Information Do you recognize yourself in this profile and would you like to know more? Please contact the hiring manager prof. dr. Kevin Williams, Full Professor at TU/e, via K.A.Williams@ remove-this. tue.nl or prof dr Martijn Heck, Full Professor at TU/e via M.Heck@ remove-this. tue.nl . Visit our website for more information about the application process . You can also contact Thomas Slegers, Senior Recruiter, via t.slegers@ remove-this. tue.nl or +3161483 5214. Curious to hear more about what it's like as a professor at TU/e? Please watch the video . Are you inspired and would like to know more about working at TU/e? Please visit our career page . Application We invite you to submit a complete application. The application should include a: Cover letter in which you describe your motivation and qualifications for the position. Curriculum vitae, including a list of your publications and the contact information of three references. Kindly note that we may reach out to references at any stage of the recruitment process. We recommend notifying your references upon submitting your application. Description of your scientific achievements and research plan for the coming five years (max 2 pages). Statement of your relevant teaching experience and goals for the coming five years (max 2 pages). Ensure that you submit all the requested application documents. Please note that incomplete applications may not be considered and could be rejected. Recruitment process: We look forward to receiving your application at the latest Friday the 4th of December 24:00h CET, 2026 . The recruitment process will include the following sequential selection rounds: Online interviews with the selection committee. Candidates’ day on our campus, including interviews and introduction program to get to know the group, the department and our university. A formal interview with a Recruitment Advisory Committee. Please note You should apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. A pre-employment screening (e.g. knowledge security check) will be part of the selection procedure. For more information on the knowledge security check, please consult the National Knowledge Security Guidelines. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Reference number: 2026/629 Apply now Share this vacancy Share Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Related vacancies Assistant/Associate Professor in Integrated Circuits for Next-Generation Communication and Sensing Systems Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Assistant Professor, Associate Professor Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 18-10-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 5.932 - € 8.199 Read more Assistant/Associate Professor In III-V Photonic Integration Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Assistant Professor, Associate Professor Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 04-12-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 8.992 Read more Assistant/Associate Professor In Physics and engineering of reliability in PICs Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Assistant Professor, Associate Professor Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 04-12-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 8.992 Read more Why join TU/e? Join the Eindhoven University of Technology and its thriving community of scientists, students, and professionals. Shape your own career as you become part of a personal university with a big impact. A university where students and lecturers know each other on a first-name basis and work together on innovative projects with real-life significance. Why TU/e? Excellent fundamental research combined with a hands-on mentality Explore our research State-of-the-art research labs Explore our labs World-leading university in cooperation with industry Explore our ecosystem Bachelor programs Master programs Admission and enrollment Working at TU/e Search staff Route & map Education Guide Intranet Cursor Navigation address De Zaale Eindhoven Phone number: +31 (0)40 247 9111 Contact Postal address PO Box 513 5600 MB Eindhoven Follow us Like TU/e on Facebook Follow TU/e on LinkedIn Follow TU/e on YouTube © 2026 TU/e Disclaimer Privacy Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor Education Education Education Why study at TU/e Bachelor College Graduate School Become a TU/e student Academy for Learning and Teaching TU/e innovation Space Professional Education Research Research Research Institutes Research Areas Research Groups Research Labs Research Projects Researchers Departments Grants & Awards Research Support Our university Our university Our university About the University Departments Calendar and events TU/e Campus Library Community Student Teams Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Support Staff PhD EngD At TU/e News and Events News and Events News and Events News overview Media relations Impact Impact Impact Cooperation with Industry Knowledge Transfer Office TU/e Participations Starting your business Intellectual Property Stay rates Brainport for Eachother TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor"
