    "https://www.tue.nl/en/working-at-tue/vacancy-overview/assistantassociate-professor-in-iii-v-photonic-integration": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor In III-V Photonic Integration",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor In III-V Photonic Integration Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies Assistant/Associate ... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies Assistant/Associate Professor In III-V Photonic Integration Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Associate Professor Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 04-12-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 8.992 Apply now Are you excited to shape the future of photonic and semiconductor technologies? Join Eindhoven University of Technology to pioneer next-generation III-V and heterogeneous photonic integration platforms that will enable breakthroughs in communications, sensing, AI, and computing. This is a unique opportunity to build an independent research program while leveraging world-class cleanroom facilities, local expertise and a leading international ecosystem in integrated photonics. Introduction Photonics is one of the fastest-growing technology domains worldwide and is rapidly becoming a key driver of innovation across communications, sensing, imaging, quantum technologies, and emerging computing systems. While integrated electronics have transformed modern society over the past decades, photonic integration is only beginning to unlock its full potential. The integration of an increased diversity of photonic components into circuits is opening new frontiers in chip design, manufacturing and applications. Improved component performance enables breakthroughs in energy efficiency, precision and bandwidth for next-generation systems based on chips. This position offers a unique opportunity to establish an independent and internationally recognized research program in III-V photonic integration. Working within one of Europe's leading photonics environments, you will develop innovative integration technologies, novel photonic devices and circuits, and future application concepts that help define the next generation of semiconductor and photonic systems. Group You will be based within the Photonic Integration (PhI) group, a European leader in photonic integrated circuits (PICs) and semiconductor process technologies. While strong interactions with existing activities are encouraged, the successful candidate will have significant freedom to develop their own distinctive research vision and establish an independent, internationally visible research program that complements and expands the group's portfolio. The group has a strong track record in indium phosphide (InP) integration, both monolithic and heterogeneous, and cleanroom-based manufacturing. This is supported by TU/e’s state-of-the-art Nanolab clean room facility including a globally leading III-V 4” InP process research line. PhI collaborates extensively with other Electrical Engineering and Applied Physics research groups and with the local and European high-tech ecosystem. The technologies developed are driving innovation in optical and wireless communications, medical and environmental sensing, imaging, and advanced computing. Job Description As an Assistant/Associate Professor, you will: Develop new research lines on photonic integrated circuit design and/or integration technologies and realize prototype photonic integrated circuit with both scientific and real-world impact. We are looking for candidates that can leverage our in-house research infrastructure and/or collaborate with external fabrication partners. Collaborate across disciplines, most notably the wider field of semicon, to explore new forms of integrated systems, enabling further miniaturization, and develop new integration paradigms. Contribute to TU/e’s educational mission by teaching and developing BSc and MSc courses, supervising PhD students and postdocs, and potentially contributing to the university’s life-long learning goals. Acquire research funding from national and European programs (e.g., Dutch, Horizon Europe, ERC) and industry collaborations. In this role, you will contribute to the ambition of the Dutch national Beethoven program to attract and educate top talent in the field of semicon, with the aim of strengthening Dutch and European industry. Job Requirements The ideal candidate: Holds a PhD in Electrical Engineering, Applied Physics, Materials Science, or a closely related field. Either has strong expertise in cleanroom based fabrication of III/V integrated photonics, or closely related technologies or has a track record in fabless circuit design and solid relations with leading foundries Has a clear and distinct research vision and is able to formulate and execute strategically Is able to thrive in a highly multi-disciplinary and team-orientated environment. Has a strong record of scientific accomplishment relative to their career stage, demonstrated through publications, awards, patents, and/or successful grant acquisition. Has an affinity with teaching, mentoring and supervision We encourage applications from talented candidates at different career stages, including early-career researchers and professionals with significant industry experience. Conditions of Employment A meaningful job in a dynamic and ambitious university, in an interdisciplinary setting and within an international network. You will work on a beautiful, green campus within walking distance of the central train station. In addition, we offer you: Salary in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities , scale 11 - 14, min. € 4,925 max. € 8,992 gross per month (on a full-time basis). In addition to your base salary, you will receive an 8% holiday allowance and an 8.3% year-end bonus, both calculated based on your annual gross base salary. Generous leave options: a standard 29 days (based on a 38 hour working week) per year that you can increase to 41 days by working two hours more per week (flexible working hours). This is prorated if you work part-time. As a TU/e employee, you participate in the ABP pension scheme, providing retirement pension and pension benefits for surviving dependents and occupational disability. TU/e pays 70% of the pension premium, while employees contribute the remaining 30%. A dedicated mentoring program to help you get to know the university and the Dutch (research) environment. A Development Track with the prospect of becoming an Associate Professor. If you have a more senior profile, a tailor-made career proposal will be considered. High-quality training programs for academic leadership and teaching. An excellent technical infrastructure, on-campus children's day care. Unlimited access to the modern on‑campus TU/e Student Sports Center at a very affordable rate. We support your wellbeing with free 24/7 access to OpenUp, providing you and your family with mental health support, expert guidance, and online training. Partially paid parental leave and an allowance for commuting, working from home and internet costs. A Staff Immigration Team is available for international candidates , as are a tax compensation scheme (the Expat Scheme ) and partner career support . On our website you can discover even more information about our conditions of employment . Build your career at TU/e! About us We are a leading international university where scientific curiosity meets a hands-on mindset. We work in an open and collaborative way with high-tech industries to tackle complex societal challenges. Our responsible and respectful approach ensures impact — today and in the future. TU/e is home to over 13,000 students and more than 7,000 staff, forming a diverse and vibrant academic community. Discover what Light Up means to TU/e in our short company video . Our university is located in Brainport Eindhoven — a world‑leading tech region with more than 7,000 high‑tech companies and strong R&D activity. Known for breakthroughs in AI, photonics, semiconductors and advanced manufacturing, Brainport is a place where technology serves people and society. Learn more about the Brainport region here . Information Do you recognize yourself in this profile and would you like to know more? Please contact the hiring manager prof. dr. Kevin Williams, Full Professor at TU/e, via K.A.Williams@ remove-this. tue.nl or prof. dr Martijn Heck, Full Professor at TU/e via M.Heck@ remove-this. tue.nl . Visit our website for more information about the application process . You can also contact Thomas Slegers, Senior Recruiter via t.slegers@ remove-this. tue.nl or +31 6 1483 5214. Curious to hear more about what it's like as a professor at TU/e? Please watch the video . Are you inspired and would like to know more about working at TU/e? Please visit our career page . Application We invite you to submit a complete application. The application should include a: Cover letter in which you describe your motivation and qualifications for the position. Curriculum vitae, including a list of your publications and the contact information of three references. Kindly note that we may reach out to references at any stage of the recruitment process. We recommend notifying your references upon submitting your application. Description of your scientific achievements and research plan for the coming five years (max 2 pages). Statement of your relevant teaching experience and goals for the coming five years (max 2 pages). Ensure that you submit all the requested application documents. Please note that incomplete applications may not be considered and could be rejected. Recruitment process: We look forward to receiving your application at the latest Friday the 4th of December 24:00h CET, 2026 . The recruitment process will include the following sequential selection rounds: Online interviews with the selection committee. Candidates’ day on our campus, including interviews and introduction program to get to know the group, the department and our university. A formal interview with a Recruitment Advisory Committee. Please note You should apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. A pre-employment screening (e.g. knowledge security check) will be part of the selection procedure. For more information on the knowledge security check, please consult the National Knowledge Security Guidelines. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Reference number: 2026/631 Apply now Share this vacancy Share Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Related vacancies Assistant/Associate Professor in Integrated Circuits for Next-Generation Communication and Sensing Systems Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Assistant Professor, Associate Professor Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 18-10-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 5.932 - € 8.199 Read more Assistant/Associate Professor In High-Frequency InP Electronics Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Assistant Professor, Associate Professor Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 04-12-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 8.992 Read more Assistant/Associate Professor In Physics and engineering of reliability in PICs Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Assistant Professor, Associate Professor Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 04-12-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 8.992 Read more Why join TU/e? Join the Eindhoven University of Technology and its thriving community of scientists, students, and professionals. Shape your own career as you become part of a personal university with a big impact. A university where students and lecturers know each other on a first-name basis and work together on innovative projects with real-life significance. Why TU/e? Excellent fundamental research combined with a hands-on mentality Explore our research State-of-the-art research labs Explore our labs World-leading university in cooperation with industry Explore our ecosystem Bachelor programs Master programs Admission and enrollment Working at TU/e Search staff Route & map Education Guide Intranet Cursor Navigation address De Zaale Eindhoven Phone number: +31 (0)40 247 9111 Contact Postal address PO Box 513 5600 MB Eindhoven Follow us Like TU/e on Facebook Follow TU/e on LinkedIn Follow TU/e on YouTube © 2026 TU/e Disclaimer Privacy Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor Education Education Education Why study at TU/e Bachelor College Graduate School Become a TU/e student Academy for Learning and Teaching TU/e innovation Space Professional Education Research Research Research Institutes Research Areas Research Groups Research Labs Research Projects Researchers Departments Grants & Awards Research Support Our university Our university Our university About the University Departments Calendar and events TU/e Campus Library Community Student Teams Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Support Staff PhD EngD At TU/e News and Events News and Events News and Events News overview Media relations Impact Impact Impact Cooperation with Industry Knowledge Transfer Office TU/e Participations Starting your business Intellectual Property Stay rates Brainport for Eachother TU/e Ima