    "https://www.tue.nl/en/working-at-tue/vacancy-overview/assistantassociate-professor-in-physics-and-engineering-of-reliability-in-pics": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor In Physics and engineering of reliability in PICs",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor In Physics and engineering of reliability in PICs Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies Assistant/Associate ... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies Assistant/Associate Professor In Physics and engineering of reliability in PICs Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Associate Professor Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 04-12-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 8.992 Apply now Are you eager to tackle some of the most fundamental reliability challenges in next-generation semiconductor and photonic technologies? Are you intrigued by why diode lasers and PICs fail? We invite ambitious researchers to join Eindhoven University of Technology and establish a world-leading research program on the mechanisms that drive reliability in integrated photonics. This is a unique opportunity to combine scientific discovery with technological impact and shape the future of photonic systems for communications, computing, sensing, and quantum applications. Introduction The Photonic Integration group (PhI) at Eindhoven University of Technology (TU/e) is seeking a high-potential candidate for a position as Assistant/Associate Professor in Physics and engineering of reliability in PICs. Photonic Integrated Circuits (PICs) are becoming essential building blocks for optical communications, sensing, quantum technologies, and emerging photonic computing systems. As PIC complexity continues to grow, reliability and lifetime increasingly determine their successful deployment. We invite applicants with expertise in reliability physics, degradation mechanisms, and lifetime assessment of semiconductor devices, and use this understanding to improve device and process design. The successful candidate will develop an internationally recognized research line focused on reliability for PICs and integrated light sources. Topics of interest include, but are not limited to, laser aging and degradation, defect propagation, reliability of heterogeneous III-V/silicon integration, high optical power effects, thermo-mechanical stress, thermal cycling, active device aging, and reliability-aware photonic design. The candidate is expected to establish experimental and modeling activities that provide fundamental insight into failure mechanisms while supporting the development of robust photonic technologies. Group The position is embedded within the Photonic Integration group in the Department of Electrical Engineering . The new faculty member will be encouraged to build their own independent research program while creating strong synergies with ongoing activities in photonic integration, integrated light sources, photonic packaging, optical communications, and emerging photonic computing. Links to comparable activities in mechanical engineering and applied physics will be encouraged. We offer a stimulating international environment, excellent research facilities, and opportunities to collaborate with leading academic and industrial partners worldwide. We welcome ambitious researchers who are eager to shape the next generation of reliable photonic technologies. Job Description As an Assistant/Associate Professor, you will: Develop an internationally recognized research program on the reliability, robustness, and lifetime of photonic integrated circuits and integrated light sources, combining experimental and modeling approaches to understand, predict, and mitigate failure mechanisms. The successful candidate will establish new research directions in failure and reliability mechanisms in integrated photonics, with a particular focus on wafer-scale and heterogeneous integration, leveraging our unique and world-leading research infrastructure. Collaborate across disciplines, most notably the wider field of semicon, to explore synergies and common physics and failure and degradation mechanisms Contribute to TU/e’s educational mission by teaching and developing BSc and MSc courses, supervising PhD students and postdocs, and potentially contribute to the university’s life-long learning goals. Acquire research funding from national and European programs (e.g., Dutch, Horizon Europe, ERC) and develop strategic collaborations with leading academic and industrial partners in photonics and semiconductors. In this role, you will contribute to the ambition of the Dutch national Beethoven program to attract and educate top talent in the field of semicon, with the aim of strengthening our industry. Job Requirements The ideal candidate: Holds a PhD in Electrical Engineering, Applied Physics, Materials Science, or a closely related field. Demonstrated expertise in reliability physics, accelerated testing and failure mechanisms of photonic, optoelectronic, or semiconductor devices Experimental and statistical approach to the analysis, assessment and understanding of high-optical-power effects, materials and interface degradation, stress mechanisms, or multiphysics reliability modeling. Is able to translate reliability insights into improvements in device, circuit or process design. Has a clear and distinct research vision and is able to formulate that and execute strategically Is able to thrive in a highly multi-disciplinary and team-focused environment. Has a strong track record of scientific achievement, as evidenced by publications, prizes, patents and/or grants, and/or equivalent proof of expertise for candidates with an industrial background. Has an affinity with teaching, mentoring and supervision We particularly welcome applicants from the broader fields of semiconductor device reliability, integrated circuit reliability, microelectronics, optoelectronics, and photonic device engineering. Prior experience in integrated photonics is welcome but not required. We are especially interested in candidates who can articulate a compelling research vision for advancing reliability methodologies and technologies for future photonic integrated systems. We encourage applications from talented candidates at different career stages, including early-career researchers and professionals with significant industry experience. Conditions of Employment A meaningful job in a dynamic and ambitious university, in an interdisciplinary setting and within an international network. You will work on a beautiful, green campus within walking distance of the central train station. In addition, we offer you: Salary in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities , scale 11 - 14, min. € 4,925 max. € 8,992 gross per month (on a full-time basis). In addition to your base salary, you will receive an 8% holiday allowance and an 8.3% year-end bonus, both calculated based on your annual gross base salary. Generous leave options: a standard 29 days (based on a 38 hour working week) per year that you can increase to 41 days by working two hours more per week (flexible working hours). This is prorated if you work part-time. As a TU/e employee, you participate in the ABP pension scheme, providing retirement pension and pension benefits for surviving dependents and occupational disability. TU/e pays 70% of the pension premium, while employees contribute the remaining 30%. A dedicated mentoring program to help you get to know the university and the Dutch (research) environment. A Development Track with the prospect of becoming an Associate Professor. If you have a more senior profile, a tailor-made career proposal will be considered. High-quality training programs for academic leadership and teaching. An excellent technical infrastructure, on-campus children's day care. Unlimited access to the modern on‑campus TU/e Student Sports Center at a very affordable rate. We support your wellbeing with free 24/7 access to OpenUp, providing you and your family with mental health support, expert guidance, and online training. Partially paid parental leave and an allowance for commuting, working from home and internet costs. A Staff Immigration Team is available for international candidates , as are a tax compensation scheme (the Expat Scheme ) and partner career support . On our website you can discover even more information about our conditions of employment . Build your career at TU/e! About us We are a leading international university where scientific curiosity meets a hands-on mindset. We work in an open and collaborative way with high-tech industries to tackle complex societal challenges. Our responsible and respectful approach ensures impact — today and in the future. TU/e is home to over 13,000 students and more than 7,000 staff, forming a diverse and vibrant academic community. Discover what Light Up means to TU/e in our short company video . Our university is located in Brainport Eindhoven — a world‑leading tech region with more than 7,000 high‑tech companies and strong R&D activity. Known for breakthroughs in AI, photonics, semiconductors and advanced manufacturing, Brainport is a place where technology serves people and society. Learn more about the Brainport region here . Information Do you recognize yourself in this profile and would you like to know more? Please contact the hiring manager prof. dr. Kevin Williams, Full Professor at TU/e, via K.A.Williams@ remove-this. tue.nl or prof dr Martijn Heck, Full Professor at TU/e via M.Heck@ remove-this. tue.nl . Visit our website for more information about the application process . You can also contact You can also contact Thomas Slegers, Senior Recruiter via t.slegers@ remove-this. tue.nl or +31 6 1483 5214. Curious to hear more about what it's like as a professor at TU/e? Please watch the video . Are you inspired and would like to know more about working at TU/e? Please visit our career page . Application We invite you to submit a complete application. The application should include a: Cover letter in which you describe your motivation and qualifications for the position. Curriculum vitae, including a list of your publications and the contact information of three references. Kindly note that we may reach out to references at any stage of the recruitment process. We recommend notifying your references upon submitting your application. Description of your scientific achievements and research plan for the coming five years (max 2 pages). Statement of your relevant teaching experience and goals for the coming five years (max 2 pages). Ensure that you submit all the requested application documents. Please note that incomplete applications may not be considered and could be rejected. Recruitment process: We look forward to receiving your application at the latest Friday the 4th of December 24:00h CET, 2026 . The recruitment process will include the following sequential selection rounds: Online interviews with the selection committee. Candidates’ day on our campus, including interviews and introduction program to get to know the group, the department and our university. A formal interview with a Recruitment Advisory Committee. Please note You should apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. A pre-employment screening (e.g. knowledge security check) will be part of the selection procedure. For more information on the knowledge security check, please consult the National Knowledge Security Guidelines. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Reference number: 2026/630 Apply now Share this vacancy Share Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Related vacancies Assistant/Associate Professor in Integrated Circuits for Next-Generation Communication and Sensing Systems Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Assistant Professor, Associate Professor Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 18-10-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 5.932 - € 8.199 Read more Assistant/Associate Professor In III-V Photonic Integration Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Assistant Professor, Associate Professor Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 04-12-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 8.992 Read more Assistant/Associate Professor In High-Frequency InP Electronics Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Assistant Professor, Associate Professor Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 04-12-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 8.992 Read more Why join TU/e? Join the Eindhoven University of Technology and its thriving community of scientists, students, and professionals. Shape your own career as you become part of a personal university with a big impact. A university where students and lecturers know each other on a first-name basis and work together on innovative projects with real-life significance. Why TU/e? Excellent fundamental research combined with a hands-on mentality Explore our research State-of-the-art research labs Explore our labs World-leading university in cooperation with industry Explore our ecosystem Bachelor programs Master programs Admission and enrollment Working at TU/e Search staff Route & map Education Guide Intranet Cursor Navigation address De Zaale Eindhoven Phone number: +31 (0)40 247 9111 Contact Postal address PO Box 513 5600 MB Eindhoven Follow us Like TU/e on Facebook Follow TU/e on Linke