    "https://www.tue.nl/en/working-at-tue/vacancy-overview/junior-advisor-research-funding": {
      "title": "Secretary / Management Assistant (0.5 fte)",
      "description": "Junior Advisor Research Funding Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies Junior Advisor Resea... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies Junior Advisor Research Funding Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: Support Organisation: Department of Biomedical Engineering Apply no later than: 08-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 3.537 - € 4.673 Apply now Introduction Do you enjoy bringing structure to complex projects and working with researchers in an innovative academic environment? Are you organized, communicative and curious about research and new technologies? Would you like to contribute to innovative research projects while developing your knowledge of research funding and project development? If so, we are looking for you. Within the Project Development Office (PDO), you will help researchers navigate the different stages of a research project, from identifying funding opportunities and preparing grant proposals to facilitating a smooth transition towards project implementation. The PDO supports researchers throughout this process, ensuring that funding opportunities are identified, proposals are well prepared and projects can move smoothly from development to implementation. We are looking for a proactive and organized Junior Project Development Officer to strengthen our research support team. In this role, you will support researchers, project coordinators and experienced Project Development Officers with grant preparation, project administration, consortium coordination and project management activities. You will help ensure that funding applications and research projects run smoothly by keeping track of deadlines, documentation, communication and administrative processes. Job Description As a Junior Advisor Research Funding, you support researchers and experienced Project Development Officers in the preparation and coordination of research proposals and projects. You help ensure that the practical, administrative and organizational aspects of funding applications are handled accurately and efficiently, keeping track of deadlines, documentation and communication. A key part of your role is keeping track of the many moving parts involved in grant applications. You coordinate input from researchers and consortium partners, organize meetings, follow up on action points, monitor deadlines, perform compliance and completeness checks, and help set up applications in funding portals such as the European Commission Funding & Tenders Portal. You also maintain application records, project documentation and internal systems, and support communication activities where needed. Once a project is awarded, you help ensure a smooth transition from proposal development to project implementation. You will support the administration and coordination of running research projects, for example by monitoring deadlines and deliverables, organizing meetings, supporting reporting and maintaining collaborative project environments such as SharePoint. Within the Project Development Office of the Department of Biomedical Engineering, you will work closely with researchers, project coordinators and colleague Project Development Officer. You will be part of a team that supports innovative research throughout the project lifecycle. This role offers an opportunity to learn about research funding, project development and the research conducted within Biomedical Engineering, while contributing to the continuous improvement of research support processes. Job Requirements We are looking for a proactive and organized colleague who is eager to learn and interested in supporting innovative research. You bring: A Bachelor's or Master's degree, preferably in Biomedical Engineering, a related field, or another relevant discipline. Strong organizational and administrative skills, with an eye for detail and the ability to keep an overview of multiple tasks and deadlines. Excellent communication skills in English, both written and verbal. A proactive and hands-on approach: you take initiative, follow up on actions and make sure things keep moving. The ability to work effectively with different stakeholders, including researchers, colleagues and external partners. An interest in research, innovation and research funding, and the curiosity to learn how research projects are developed and funded. Affinity with digital tools and new technologies, and an interest in exploring how AI and other tools can improve the way we work. Experience with academic research, project management, research funding, or tools such as Microsoft Teams, SharePoint and online grant submission systems is a plus, but not required. If you are concerned that you don’t meet all the requirements sufficiently, but the job does excite you, then be sure to respond, we would love to look at your profile. Conditions of Employment An exciting position within an international yet personal university. You are right in the middle of the students, on a green campus within walking distance of the central station. Besides beautiful architecture, you will find varied workplaces and excellent sports facilities. We also offer you: Salary in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities , starting scale 8, ranging from €3.537 to €4.673. gross base salary per month (full-time), depending on your knowledge and experience. In addition to your base salary, you will receive an 8% holiday allowance and an 8.3% year-end bonus, both calculated based on your annual gross base salary. Generous leave options: a standard 29 days (based on a 38 hour working week) per year that you can increase to 41 days by working two hours more per week (flexible working hours). This is prorated if you work part-time. As a TU/e employee, you participate in the ABP pension scheme, providing retirement pension and pension benefits for surviving dependents and occupational disability. TU/e pays 70% of the pension premium, while employees contribute the remaining 30%. A favorable arrangement for more holidays or a sabbatical. A selection model for additional fringe benefits. Working hours in consultation to support a healthy work-life balance, with the opportunity to work from home occasionally where the work allows. Unlimited access to the modern on‑campus TU/e Student Sports Center at an exceptionally affordable rate. We support your wellbeing with free 24/7 access to OpenUp, providing you and your family with mental health support, expert guidance, and online training. Scope for your talent with advancement prospects and excellent development opportunities such as mentoring, workshops and coaching. Partially paid parental leave and reimbursement for commuting expenses, working from home and the internet. On our website you can discover even more information about our conditions of employment . Build on your career at TU/e! About us The Department of Biomedical Engineering offers top-level education and research in one of the most relevant and exciting scientific disciplines of the 21st century: engineering health. In combining engineering and life sciences, through challenge-based learning and a multidisciplinary approach in collaboration with hospitals, industry and others, the department addresses the great challenges of the future, striving to improve healthcare and society as a whole. We are a leading international university where scientific curiosity meets a hands-on mindset. We work in an open and collaborative way with high-tech industries to tackle complex societal challenges. Our responsible and respectful approach ensures impact — today and in the future. TU/e is home to over 13,000 students and more than 7,000 staff, forming a diverse and vibrant academic community. Discover what Light Up means to TU/e in our short company video . Our university is located in Braintport Eindhoven and part of a strong and diverse ecosystem of clinical centres, innovative SMEs and leading international companies. This close collaboration creates opportunities to connect research, technology and clinical practice, and to contribute to innovations that have a meaningful impact on society. Learn more about the Brainport region here . Information Do you recognize yourself in this profile and would you like to have more information about the position, please contact the hiring manager:  Steffie Hermans – Beijnsberger, s.hermans.beijnsberger@ remove-this. tue.nl . Visit our website for more information about the application process . You can also contact Ivo Uitdenbogaart, Recruiter, i.uitdenbogaart@ remove-this. tue.nl or +31 40 247 3299. Are you inspired and would like to know more about working at TU/e? Please visit our career page. Application If you are interested, please use the ‘apply’ button to send us your CV and letter of application with your motivation and a description of your qualifications. Ensure that you submit all the requested application documents. We give priority to complete applications. Screening of candidates begins as soon as applications are received and continues until the position is filled. Where applicable, internal candidates will be given priority over external candidates where they are equally suitable. We look forward to receiving your application! Please note You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. Applications will be reviewed as soon as possible. A pre-employment screening (e.g. knowledge security check) can be part of the selection procedure. For more information on the knowledge security check, please consult the National Knowledge Security Guidelines . Important for non-EU applicants: Please be aware that for this position, specific residence permit requirements apply. If you are a non-EU national, you may not be eligible to legally work in this role under current Dutch immigration regulations. We strongly advise you to contact our Staff Immigration Team ( staffimmigration@ remove-this. tue.nl ) before applying to check your eligibility and to receive further guidance. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Reference number: 2026/622 Apply now Share this vacancy Share Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Related vacancies Secretary / Management Assistant (0.5 fte) Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: Support Organisation: Department of Chemical Engineering and Chemistry Apply no later than: 01-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.5 FTE Salary: € 3.173 - € 4.159 Read more Sr. Projectmanager Vastgoed Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: Support Organisation: Campus and Facilities Apply no later than: 31-10-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 5.932 - € 7.573 Read more Senior Projectleider Vastgoed Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: Support Organisation: Campus and Facilities Apply no later than: 31-10-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 6.682 Read more Why join TU/e? Join the Eindhoven University of Technology and its thriving community of scientists, students, and professionals. Shape your own career as you become part of a personal university with a big impact. A university where students and lecturers know each other on a first-name basis and work together on innovative projects with real-life significance. Why TU/e? Excellent fundamental research combined with a hands-on mentality Explore our research State-of-the-art research labs Explore our labs World-leading university in cooperation with industry Explore our ecosystem Bachelor programs Master programs Admission and enrollment Working at TU/e Search staff Route & map Education Guide Intranet Cursor Navigation address De Zaale Eindhoven Phone number: +31 (0)40 247 9111 Contact Postal address PO Box 513 5600 MB Eindhoven Follow us Like TU/e on Facebook Follow TU/e on LinkedIn Follow TU/e on YouTube © 2026 TU/e Disclaimer Privacy Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor Education Education Education Why study at TU/e Bachelor College Graduate School Become a TU/e student Academy for Learning and Teaching TU/e innovation Space Professional Education Research Research Research Institutes Research Areas Research Groups Research Labs Research Projects Researchers Departments Grants & Awards Research Support Our university Our university Our university About the University Departments Calendar and events TU/e Campus Library Community Student Teams Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Support Staff PhD EngD At TU/e News and Events News and Events News and Events News overview Media relations Impact Impact Impact Cooperation with Industry Knowledge Transfer Office TU/e Participations Starting your business Intellectual Property Stay rates Brainport for Eachother TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor"
