    "https://www.tue.nl/en/working-at-tue/vacancy-overview/postdoc-on-real-time-emt-modelling-of-future-mvlv-distribution-systems-utopys": {
      "title": "Postdoc on Real-Time EMT Modelling of Future MV/LV Distribution Systems (UTOPYS)",
      "description": "Postdoc on Real-Time EMT Modelling of Future MV/LV Distribution Systems (UTOPYS) Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies Postdoc on Real-Time... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies Postdoc on Real-Time EMT Modelling of Future MV/LV Distribution Systems (UTOPYS) Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Postdoctorate Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 14-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.422 - € 5.760 Apply now Introduction The UTOPYS project is a state-of-the-art Large-Scale Research Infrastructure (LSRI) initiative funded by the Dutch Research Council (NWO). UTOPYS aims to revolutionize the science of power systems by creating a state-of-the-art real-time electromagnetic transient (EMT) simulator. This infrastructure will enable unprecedented research into the dynamics, control, and market design of future power systems dominated by renewables, power electronics, and cyber-physical interactions. As a consortium of leading Dutch universities and research institutes (TU Delft, TU Eindhoven, University of Twente, University of Groningen, CWI, Utrecht University, Erasmus University Rotterdam, and Radboud University), UTOPYS will drive scientific breakthroughs in mathematical modeling, control strategies, and policy/regulatory frameworks for complex power systems. We are seeking a motivated and creative postdoctoral researcher to join our team and contribute to the development, validation, and application of the UTOPYS infrastructure. Job Description The energy transition is reshaping power systems at an unprecedented pace, introducing complexity that challenges our fundamental understanding of grid stability, control, and market design. As renewable energy, power electronics, and digitalization dominate the grid, we face unexplained blackouts, wide-area oscillations, and cyber-physical vulnerabilities that traditional theories cannot address. The question is no longer if these challenges will arise, but how we can predict, mitigate, and design systems to handle them. This is where you come in. In this job, you will join UTOPYS to establish the foundations for groundbreaking research on the one of the largest real-time electromagnetic transient (EMT) simulator. The UTOPYS consortium includes 8 Dutch universities and research institutes, along with industry partners like power system operators. You will have access to cutting-edge facilities, including the real-time power-hardware-in-the-loop simulators within the EES Smart Grid Lab at TU/e and the Electrical Sustainable Power Lab at TU Delft. Your role will focus on developing, validating, and simulating realistic EMT reference models of future MV/LV distribution systems assembled from the TU/e component library using the UTOPYS infrastructure. You’ll create high-fidelity models focused on how grid-operator assets are operated together, including protection schemes and their coordination across the network, DSO operating paradigms such as voltage and congestion management, reconfiguration, curtailment and the use of flexibility, and the provision of power system ancillary services from within the MV system including frequency control, voltage/reactive power control, black start capabilities and fault ride through, to enable research for uncovering the root causes of instability, blackouts, and other emergent power system phenomena. Your research will directly inform new mathematical frameworks, control strategies, and market designs, ensuring that the grids of tomorrow are stable, fair, and resilient. Job Requirements Motivated researcher, with a PhD in electrical power engineering research, or a comparable domain. Ability to conduct high quality academic research, reflected in demonstratable outputs. A team player who enjoys coaching PhD and Master's students and working in a dynamic, interdisciplinary team. A proven ability to manage complex projects to completion on schedule. Excellent (written and verbal) proficiency in English, good communication and leadership skills. Conditions of Employment A meaningful job in a dynamic and ambitious university, in an interdisciplinary setting and within an international network. You will work on a beautiful, green campus within walking distance of the central train station. In addition, we offer you: Full-time employment for 2 years. Salary in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities , scale 10, ranging from € 4,422 (step 4) to € 5,760 gross base salary per month (full-time). In addition to your base salary, you will receive an 8% holiday allowance and an 8.3% year-end bonus, both calculated based on your annual gross base salary. Generous leave options: a standard 29 days (based on a 38 hour working week) per year that you can increase to 41 days by working two hours more per week (flexible working hours). This is prorated if you work part-time. As a TU/e employee, you participate in the ABP pension scheme, providing retirement pension and pension benefits for surviving dependents and occupational disability. TU/e pays 70% of the pension premium, while employees contribute the remaining 30%. High-quality training programs on general skills, didactics and topics related to research and valorization. An excellent technical infrastructure, and on-campus children's day care. Unlimited access to the modern on‑campus TU/e Student Sports Center at an exceptionally affordable rate. We support your wellbeing with free 24/7 access to OpenUp, providing you and your family with mental health support, expert guidance, and online training. Partially paid parental leave and an allowance for commuting, working from home and internet costs. A TU/e Postdoc Association that helps you to build a stronger and broader academic and personal network, and offers tailored support, training and workshops. A Staff Immigration Team is available for international candidates, as are a tax compensation scheme (the Expat Scheme ) and a compensation for moving expenses. On our website you can discover even more information about our conditions of employment . Build on your career at TU/e! About us We are a leading international university where scientific curiosity meets a hands-on mindset. We work in an open and collaborative way with high-tech industries to tackle complex societal challenges. Our responsible and respectful approach ensures impact — today and in the future. TU/e is home to over 13,000 students and more than 7,000 staff, forming a diverse and vibrant academic community. Discover what Light Up means to TU/e in our short company video . Our university is located in Brainport Eindhoven — a world‑leading tech region with more than 7,000 high‑tech companies and strong R&D activity. Known for breakthroughs in AI, photonics, semiconductors and advanced manufacturing, Brainport is a place where technology serves people and society. Learn more about the Brainport region here . The mission of the Department of Electrical Engineering is to acquire, share and transfer knowledge and understanding in the whole field of Electrical Engineering through education, research and valorization. We work towards a ‘Smart Sustainable Society’, a ‘Connected World’, and a healthy humanity (‘Care & Cure’). Activities share an application-oriented character, a high degree of complexity and a large synergy between multiple facets of the field. Research is carried out into the applications of electromagnetic phenomena in all forms of energy conversion, telecommunication and electrical signal processing. Existing and new electrical components and systems are analyzed, designed and built. The Electrical Engineering department takes its inspiration from contacts with high-tech industry in the direct surrounding region and beyond. The department is innovative and has international ambitions and partnerships. The result is a challenging and inspiring setting in which socially relevant issues are addressed. Information Do you recognize yourself in this profile and would you like to know more? Please contact the hiring manager Niels Blaauwbroek, Assistant Professor, n.blaauwbroek@ remove-this. tue.nl . Visit our website for more information about the application process . You can also contact HRServices.ee@ remove-this. tue.nl . Are you inspired and would like to know more about working at TU/e? Please visit our career page. Application We invite you to submit a complete application using the apply-button. The application should include a: Cover letter in which you describe your motivation and qualifications for the position. Curriculum vitae, including a list of your publications and the contact information of three references. Kindly note that we may reach out to references at any stage of the recruitment process. We recommend notifying your references upon submitting your application. List of up to five self-selected ‘best publications’. Ensure that you submit all the requested application documents. Please note that incomplete applications may not be considered and could be rejected. We look forward to receiving your application and will screen it as soon as possible. The vacancy will remain open until the position is filled. Please note You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. A pre-employment screening (e.g. knowledge security check) can be part of the selection procedure. For more information on the knowledge security check, please consult the National Knowledge Security Guidelines . Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Reference number: 2026/638 Apply now Share this vacancy Share Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Related vacancies Postdoc In Algebraic Graph Theory and Applications Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Postdoctorate Organisation: Department of Mathematics and Computer Science Apply no later than: 31-12-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.422 - € 5.760 Read more PostDoc on Targeted Proteomics for Protein Biomarker Standardization Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Postdoctorate Organisation: Department of Biomedical Engineering Apply no later than: 05-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.422 - € 5.760 Read more Postdoc In assessing the structural performance of polymers in an alkaline electrolyzer Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Postdoctorate Organisation: Department of Mechanical Engineering Apply no later than: 16-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.422 - € 5.760 Read more Why join TU/e? Join the Eindhoven University of Technology and its thriving community of scientists, students, and professionals. Shape your own career as you become part of a personal university with a big impact. A university where students and lecturers know each other on a first-name basis and work together on innovative projects with real-life significance. Why TU/e? Excellent fundamental research combined with a hands-on mentality Explore our research State-of-the-art research labs Explore our labs World-leading university in cooperation with industry Explore our ecosystem Bachelor programs Master programs Admission and enrollment Working at TU/e Search staff Route & map Education Guide Intranet Cursor Navigation address De Zaale Eindhoven Phone number: +31 (0)40 247 9111 Contact Postal address PO Box 513 5600 MB Eindhoven Follow us Like TU/e on Facebook Follow TU/e on LinkedIn Follow TU/e on YouTube © 2026 TU/e Disclaimer Privacy Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor Education Education Education Why study at TU/e Bachelor College Graduate School Become a TU/e student Academy for Learning and Teaching TU/e innovation Space Professional Education Research Research Research Institutes Research Areas Research Groups Research Labs Research Projects Researchers Departments Grants & Awards Research Support Our university Our university Our university About the University Departments Calendar and events TU/e Campus Library Community Student Teams Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Support Staff PhD EngD At TU/e News and Events News and Events News and Events News overview Media relations Impact Impact Impact Cooperation with Industry Knowledge Transfer Office TU/e Participations Starting your business Intellectual Property Stay rates Brainport for Eachother TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor"
    },
    "https://www.tue.nl/en/working-at-tue/vacancy-overview/secretaresse-binnen-de-faculteit-bouwkunde-07-fte": {
      "title": "Secretary / Management Assistant (0.5 fte)",
      "description": "Secretaresse binnen de Faculteit Bouwkunde (0,7 fte) Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies Secretaresse binnen ... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies Secretaresse binnen de Faculteit Bouwkunde (0,7 fte) Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: Support Organisation:\n                \n                Unknown Apply no later than: 31-10-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.7 FTE Salary: € 3.202 - € 4.159 Apply now Introductie De Faculteit Bouwkunde huisvest een uniek breed spectrum van disciplinaire kennis op het gebied van architectuur, stedenbouw en bouwtechnologie. Wij werken op verschillende schaalniveaus, van materialen tot gebouwen tot steden, en besteden aandacht aan de impact van ontwerp en technologie op de mens. Onze missie is het opleiden van studenten en het bevorderen van wetenschap en technologie vanuit het perspectief van de gebouwde omgeving en ten behoeve van de maatschappij als geheel. Wij integreren onderwijs, onderzoek en ontwerp in één onderwijsprogramma om studenten in staat te stellen thought leaders te worden, om steden en de bouwindustrie (opnieuw) vorm te geven en bij te dragen aan grote maatschappelijke uitdagingen. De afdeling telt ongeveer 260 academische medewerkers, waaronder ongeveer 190 PhD's, EngD’s en Postdocs, georganiseerd in vier disciplinaire eenheden. Wetenschappers binnen de eenheden worden gestimuleerd om over de grenzen van hun eigen vakgebied heen samen te werken in interdisciplinair onderzoek en onderwijs rond de thema's: energietransitie, duurzaamheid en inclusiviteit. De faculteit heeft in 2022 haar nieuwe strategisch plan gepresenteerd, en is volop in ontwikkeling op onderwijs, onderzoek en haar bedrijfsvoering. Om deze doorontwikkeling goed te ondersteunen, zoekt de unit AUDE binnen de faculteit een secretaresse ter vervanging van de huidige secretaresse. Het secretariaat (2 secretaresses binnen de unit AUDE) biedt ondersteuning aan de unitvoorzitter, de deputy-unitvoorzitter, hoogleraren en staf binnen de unit. De twee secretaresses werken hierbij nauw samen en zorgen gezamenlijk voor een efficiënte en continue ondersteuning van de unit. Functieomschrijving Als secretaresse vervul je de volgende taken: Je bent eerstelijns aanspreekpunt in de faculteit voor interne en externe relaties; Je verleent ondersteuning aan medewerkers op procesmatig, administratief en/of organisatorisch gebied; Je coördineert administratieve zaken bij academische plechtigheden voor de unit AUDE; Je geeft secretariële ondersteuning aan de hoogleraren binnen de unit AUDE als geheel, waarbij je secuur bent en het hoofd koel kunt houden in tijden van drukte; Je bereidt verschillende vergaderingen voor, werkt stukken uit en notuleert bij verschillende vergaderingen (voertaal Engels); Je organiseert en ondersteunt unit brede activiteiten; Je werkt in een gedeeld secretariaat en stemt werkzaamheden, prioriteiten en vervanging proactief af met je collega-secretaresse om de continuïteit van de ondersteuning binnen de unit te waarborgen; Je vervangt je collega’s binnen de gehele faculteit bij afwezigheid. Functie-eisen Wij zoeken een ervaren enthousiaste, betrokken, integere en zelfstandige en samenwerkingsgerichte teamplayer die voldoet aan de volgende eisen: Senior kennis en ervaring van het secretaressewerk, bij voorkeur binnen een universiteit en een organisatie in ontwikkeling (ten minste 5 jaar ervaring in een vergelijkbare positie); Ervaring met het zelfstandig stroomlijnen van (administratieve) processen, gebruik makend van de mogelijkheden binnen de TU/e systemen (TU/e Insite, Verseon, iBabs, MS Teams, Valid Sign, MS Office, Oracle etc.) Goede beheersing van de Nederlandse en Engelse taal in woord en geschrift; Stress bestendig en snel kunnen schakelen tussen verschillende taken en opdrachten (om kunnen gaan met heel diverse taken); In staat zijn om snel de organisatiestructuur, verhoudingen en procedures eigen te maken; Flexibele, servicegerichte en proactieve houding; Goede sociale, diplomatieke en communicatieve vaardigheden. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Een boeiende positie binnen een internationale en tegelijkertijd persoonlijke universiteit. Je zit midden tussen de studenten, op een groene campus op loopafstand van het centraal station. Daarnaast bieden we jou: Een bruto maandsalaris van minimaal € 3.202,- tot maximaal € 4.159,- bij een fulltime dienstverband, afhankelijk van jouw kennis en ervaring (schaal 7 cao Nederlandse Universiteiten ). Naast je basissalaris ontvang je een vakantietoeslag van 8% en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%, beide berekend over je jaarlijkse bruto basissalaris. Ruime verlofmogelijkheden: standaard 29 vakantiedagen per jaar (op basis van een werkweek van 38 uur). Dit aantal kun je verhogen naar 41 dagen door wekelijks twee uur extra te werken (flexibele werktijden). Werk je parttime, dan wordt het aantal verlofdagen naar rato berekend. Als medewerker van de TU/e neem je deel aan de pensioenregeling van ABP. Deze regeling voorziet in een ouderdoms-, een nabestaanden- en een arbeidsongeschiktheidspensioen. De TU/e betaalt 70% van de pensioenpremie; medewerkers dragen de overige 30% bij. Een gunstige regeling voor extra verlofdagen of een sabbatical. Een keuzemodel voor extra secundaire arbeidsvoorwaarden. Werktijden in overleg voor een optimale werk-privé balans. Toegang tot het moderne sportcentrum op de TU/e‑campus tegen een uitzonderlijk voordelig tarief. We ondersteunen je welzijn met gratis 24/7 toegang tot OpenUp, waarmee jij en je gezin toegang hebben tot mentale ondersteuning, deskundig advies en online trainingen. Ruimte voor jouw talent met doorgroeikansen en uitstekende ontwikkelmogelijkheden , zoals mentoring, workshops en coaching. Deels betaald ouderschapsverlof en een vergoeding voor reiskosten woon-werkverkeer, thuiswerken en internet. Op onze website ontdek je nog meer informatie over onze arbeidsvoorwaarden . Bouw verder aan je carrière bij de TU/e! Over ons Wij zijn een toonaangevende internationale universiteit waar wetenschappelijke nieuwsgierigheid samenkomt met een pragmatische, hands‑on mentaliteit. We werken op een open en samenwerkingsgerichte manier met hightechindustrieën om complexe maatschappelijke uitdagingen aan te pakken. Onze verantwoordelijke en respectvolle benadering zorgt voor impact — vandaag én in de toekomst. TU/e is de thuisbasis van meer dan 13.000 studenten en ruim 7.000 medewerkers, samen een diverse en bruisende academische gemeenschap. Ontdek wat Light Up voor de TU/e betekent in onze korte video . Onze universiteit bevindt zich in Brainport Eindhoven — een wereldwijd toonaangevende technologieregio met meer dan 7.000 hightechbedrijven en sterke R&D‑activiteiten. Brainport staat bekend om doorbraken op het gebied van AI, fotonica, halfgeleiders en geavanceerde maakindustrie. Het is een regio waar technologie in dienst staat van mensen en de samenleving. Meer informatie over de Brainport‑regio vind je hier . Informatie Herken jij jezelf in dit profiel en wil je meer informatie over de functie? Neem dan contact op met de vacaturehouder: Dr Deniz Ikiz, Deputy Unit Chair, d.ikiz.kaya@ remove-this. tue.nl . Bezoek onze website voor meer informatie over het sollicitatieproces . Je kunt hierover ook contact opnemen met Jennifer Berkhout-Dekker, HR-adviseur, HRadviceBE@ remove-this. tue.nl of +31 40 247 2215; of met Helen van Mierlo, hvmierlo@ remove-this. tue.nl . Nieuwsgierig geworden? Op www.tue.nl/jobs vind je meer over werken bij de TU/e. Sollicitatie Ben je geïnteresseerd? Via de solliciteerknop ontvangen we graag je CV en brief met motivatie en omschrijving van je kwalificaties. Zorg ervoor dat je alle gevraagde documenten toevoegt. Wij geven voorrang aan complete sollicitaties. De screening van kandidaten begint zodra de sollicitaties zijn ontvangen en gaat door totdat de vacature is ingevuld. Indien van toepassing, krijgen interne kandidaten bij gelijke geschiktheid voorrang op externe kandidaten. We kijken uit naar je sollicitatie! Let op Je kunt online solliciteren. Sollicitaties die per e-mail en/of post worden verstuurd, worden niet in behandeling genomen. Een voorafgaande screening (bijvoorbeeld een Verklaring omtrent Gedrag of kennisveiligheidscheck) kan onderdeel zijn van de selectieprocedure. Voor meer informatie over de kennisveiligheidscheck, raadpleeg de Nationale Richtlijnen Kennisveiligheid . Wij verzoeken je geen contact met ons op te nemen voor ongevraagde diensten. Reference number: 2026/634 Apply now Share this vacancy Share Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Related vacancies Secretary / Management Assistant (0.5 fte) Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: Support Organisation: Department of Chemical Engineering and Chemistry Apply no later than: 01-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.5 FTE Salary: € 3.173 - € 4.159 Read more Sr. Projectmanager Vastgoed Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: Support Organisation: Campus and Facilities Apply no later than: 31-10-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 5.932 - € 7.573 Read more Senior Projectleider Vastgoed Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: Support Organisation: Campus and Facilities Apply no later than: 31-10-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 6.682 Read more Why join TU/e? Join the Eindhoven University of Technology and its thriving community of scientists, students, and professionals. Shape your own career as you become part of a personal university with a big impact. A university where students and lecturers know each other on a first-name basis and work together on innovative projects with real-life significance. Why TU/e? Excellent fundamental research combined with a hands-on mentality Explore our research State-of-the-art research labs Explore our labs World-leading university in cooperation with industry Explore our ecosystem Bachelor programs Master programs Admission and enrollment Working at TU/e Search staff Route & map Education Guide Intranet Cursor Navigation address De Zaale Eindhoven Phone number: +31 (0)40 247 9111 Contact Postal address PO Box 513 5600 MB Eindhoven Follow us Like TU/e on Facebook Follow TU/e on LinkedIn Follow TU/e on YouTube © 2026 TU/e Disclaimer Privacy Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor Education Education Education Why study at TU/e Bachelor College Graduate School Become a TU/e student Academy for Learning and Teaching TU/e innovation Space Professional Education Research Research Research Institutes Research Areas Research Groups Research Labs Research Projects Researchers Departments Grants & Awards Research Support Our university Our university Our university About the University Departments Calendar and events TU/e Campus Library Community Student Teams Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Support Staff PhD EngD At TU/e News and Events News and Events News and Events News overview Media relations Impact Impact Impact Cooperation with Industry Knowledge Transfer Office TU/e Participations Starting your business Intellectual Property Stay rates Brainport for Eachother TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor"
