    "https://www.tue.nl/en/working-at-tue/vacancy-overview/cleanroom-teaching-support-and-lab-manager-08-10-fte": {
      "title": "Cleanroom teaching support and lab manager 0,8-1,0 fte",
      "description": "Cleanroom teaching support and lab manager 0,8-1,0 fte Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies Cleanroom teaching s... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies Cleanroom teaching support and lab manager 0,8-1,0 fte Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: Support Organisation: Department of Applied Physics and Science Education Apply no later than: 29-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 3.706 - € 5.760 Apply now Introduction Are you passionate about training future scientists and engineers in semicon? Do you enjoy working in a high-tech cleanroom environment and supporting students in their learning? We are looking for a colleague to help operate a unique hands-on learning facility and contribute to educational activities that connect students with the rapidly evolving microelectronics industry. Job Description We are looking for a cleanroom teaching support scientist/engineer who is passionate about practical education and wants to contribute to expanding hands-on training activities within our cleanroom facilities. This position plays a key role in strengthening TU/e’s contribution to the Dutch Beethoven Plan, aimed at scaling up semiconductor talent to meet the growing demands of the high-tech industry. In this role, you will be part of the Education and Student Affairs (ESA) team within the Department of Applied Physics and Science Education (APSE). The ESA APSE team provides educational support for all Bachelor’s and Master’s programs within the department. Your role will focus specifically on supporting education in Applied Physics, including the Bachelor’s program in Applied Physics, the Master’s program in Applied Physics, and the Master’s program in Science and Technology of Nuclear Fusion. You will help create a safe, engaging, and challenging learning environment where students gain practical experience in micro/nanofabrication processes. You will be working closely with academic staff and technical teams to support educational activities at Bachelor and Master levels taking place in the NanoLab ( https://www.tue.nl/en/research/research-groups/nanolabtue/nanolabtue ) and Educational Cleanrooms. A key part of the role involves managing the educational cleanroom facilities and supporting their daily operation. This facility is part of the Flux CBL Labs, a joint initiative of the Departments of Applied Physics and Science Education (APSE) and Electrical Engineering (EE), where students have access to advanced fabrication and characterization equipment. You will work in close collaboration with the Program Director for Applied Physics education, the manager ESA APSE, teaching staff and the Flux CBL Labs Team, as well as the NanoLab team. As a member of the ESA APSE team, you will report to the Manager ESA APSE. Your responsibilities In this role, you will: Support cleanroom educational activities (0.5-0.6 fte): Support practical courses and hands-on training in a cleanroom environment. Teach course modules or laboratory activities related to micro/nanofabrication and device processing. Contribute to course content development and delivery in collaboration with responsible teacher(s). Train teaching assistants and students in the safe and effective use of selected cleanroom equipment. Organize and help coordinate educational activities for Bachelor and Master courses in the cleanroom facilities, acting as a liaison with NanoLab. Manage the educational cleanroom in Flux CBL Labs (0.3-0.4 fte): Oversee the day-to-day operation of the facility. Maintain, troubleshoot, and coordinate maintenance of cleanroom equipment. Manage consumables and waste handling. Support the development and implementation of safety documentation, including risk assessments, work instructions, and emergency procedures. Schedule educational activities, student projects, and facility usage. Organize and deliver user training in cleanroom safety, procedures, and equipment operation. Contribute to the further development of the facility, including new processes, equipment, and educational activities. Job Requirements We are looking for a candidate who meets the following requirements: Holds a MSc or PhD in Electrical Engineering, Applied Physics, Nanotechnology, Microelectronics, or a closely related field. Has proven experience working with cleanroom or semiconductor/microfabrication techniques (e.g. lithography, deposition, etching, inspection), preferably in an academic or high-tech setting. Has preferably some experience working in the Nanolab at TU/e. Has an affinity with education and an interest in supporting students and teachers in a learning-oriented environment. Has proven didactic qualities and the ability to pass on knowledge and skills to students; Is willing to work on developing practical educational activities within a team. Has a proactive and hands-on attitude: you enjoy being present in the lab, solving practical issues, and improving processes. Has strong awareness of safety and the discipline to enforce and promote safe working practices. Has a good command of English, both orally and in writing. Has the ability to work both independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team, with a service-oriented mindset. If you are concerned that you don’t meet all the requirements sufficiently, but the job does excite you, then be sure to respond, we would love to look at your profile. Conditions of Employment An exciting position within an international yet personal university. You are right in the middle of the students, on a green campus within walking distance of the central station. Besides beautiful architecture, you will find varied workplaces and excellent sports facilities. We also offer you: A 0,8-1,0 FTE temporary position of one year with the prospect of a subsequent three-year extension, provided performance meets expectations. Salary in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities , scale 10, ranging from € 3,706 to € 5,760 gross base salary per month (full-time), depending on your knowledge and experience. In addition to your base salary, you will receive an 8% holiday allowance and an 8.3% year-end bonus, both calculated based on your annual gross base salary. Generous leave options: a standard 29 days (based on a 38 hour working week) per year that you can increase to 41 days by working two hours more per week (flexible working hours). This is prorated if you work part-time. As a TU/e employee, you participate in the ABP pension scheme, providing retirement pension and pension benefits for surviving dependents and occupational disability. TU/e pays 70% of the pension premium, while employees contribute the remaining 30%. A favorable arrangement for more holidays or a sabbatical. A selection model for additional fringe benefits. Working hours in consultation for an optimal work-life balance. Unlimited access to the modern on‑campus TU/e Student Sports Center at an exceptionally affordable rate. We support your wellbeing with free 24/7 access to OpenUp, providing you and your family with mental health support, expert guidance, and online training. Scope for your talent with advancement prospects and excellent development opportunities such as mentoring, workshops and coaching. Partially paid parental leave and reimbursement for commuting expenses, working from home and the internet. On our website you can discover even more information about our conditions of employment . Build on your career at TU/e! About us We are a leading international university where scientific curiosity meets a hands-on mindset. We work in an open and collaborative way with high-tech industries to tackle complex societal challenges. Our responsible and respectful approach ensures impact — today and in the future. TU/e is home to over 13,000 students and more than 7,000 staff, forming a diverse and vibrant academic community. Discover what Light Up means to TU/e in our short company video . Our university is located in Brainport Eindhoven — a world‑leading tech region with more than 7,000 high‑tech companies and strong R&D activity. Known for breakthroughs in AI, photonics, semiconductors and advanced manufacturing, Brainport is a place where technology serves people and society. Learn more about the Brainport region here . The Department of Applied Physics and Science Education is a research-driven department housing high-quality educational programs, all featuring strong connections between research and education. Our research is clustered in three focal areas: Fluids, Bio and Soft Matter (FBSM); Plasmas and Beams (PB); and Nano, Quantum and Photonics (NQP). Our shared ambition is to equip the next generation of ‘engineers of the future’ with the knowledge and the skills they will need to impact science, innovation, and society, from regional to global scales. Information Do you recognize yourself in this profile and would you like to have more information about the position, please contact prof. Wouter Ellenbroek (program director APSE): w.g.ellenbroek@ remove-this. tue.nl . Visit our website for more information about the application process . You can also contact HR Advisor Stefan van Luijk: s.h.v.luijk@ remove-this. tue.nl . Are you inspired and would like to know more about working at TU/e? Please visit our career page. Application If you are interested, please use the ‘apply’ button to send us your CV and letter of application with your motivation and a description of your qualifications. Ensure that you submit all the requested application documents. We give priority to complete applications. Screening of candidates begins as soon as applications are received and continues until the position is filled. Where applicable, internal candidates will be given priority over external candidates where they are equally suitable. We look forward to receiving your application! Please note You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. A pre-employment screening (e.g. knowledge security check) can be part of the selection procedure. For more information on the knowledge security check, please consult the National Knowledge Security Guidelines . Important for non-EU applicants: Please be aware that for this position, specific residence permit requirements apply. If you are a non-EU national, you may not be eligible to legally work in this role under current Dutch immigration regulations. We strongly advise you to contact our Staff Immigration Team ( staffimmigration@ remove-this. tue.nl ) before applying to check your eligibility and to receive further guidance. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Reference number: 2026/636 Apply now Share this vacancy Share Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Related vacancies Secretary / Management Assistant (0.5 fte) Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: Support Organisation: Department of Chemical Engineering and Chemistry Apply no later than: 01-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.5 FTE Salary: € 3.173 - € 4.159 Read more Senior Projectleider Vastgoed Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: Support Organisation: Campus and Facilities Apply no later than: 31-10-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 6.682 Read more Projectleider Vastgoed Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: Support Organisation: Campus and Facilities Apply no later than: 15-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 3.873 - € 5.760 Read more Why join TU/e? Join the Eindhoven University of Technology and its thriving community of scientists, students, and professionals. Shape your own career as you become part of a personal university with a big impact. A university where students and lecturers know each other on a first-name basis and work together on innovative projects with real-life significance. Why TU/e? Excellent fundamental research combined with a hands-on mentality Explore our research State-of-the-art research labs Explore our labs World-leading university in cooperation with industry Explore our ecosystem Bachelor programs Master programs Admission and enrollment Working at TU/e Search staff Route & map Education Guide Intranet Cursor Navigation address De Zaale Eindhoven Phone number: +31 (0)40 247 9111 Contact Postal address PO Box 513 5600 MB Eindhoven Follow us Like TU/e on Facebook Follow TU/e on LinkedIn Follow TU/e on YouTube © 2026 TU/e Disclaimer Privacy Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor Education Education Education Why study at TU/e Bachelor College Graduate School Become a TU/e student Academy for Learning and Teaching TU/e innovation Space Professional Education Research Research Research Institutes Research Areas Research Groups Research Labs Research Projects Researchers Departments Grants & Awards Research Support Our university Our university Our university About the University Departments Calendar and events TU/e Campus Library Community Student Teams Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Support Staff PhD EngD At TU/e News and Events News and Events News and Events News overview Media relations Impact Impact Impact Cooperation with Industry Knowledge Transfer Office TU/e Participations Starting your business Intellectual Property Stay rates Brainport for Eachother TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor"
    },
    "https://www.tue.nl/en/working-at-tue/vacancy-overview/director-finance-control": {
      "title": "Director Finance & Control",
      "description": "Director Finance & Control Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies Director Finance & C... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies Director Finance & Control Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: Finance Organisation: Finance and Control Apply no later than: 09-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 8.309 - € 10.815 Apply now Finance and Control (F&C) is responsible for all financial and economic management of TU/e and affiliated institutions. This includes making and executing financial policy, advising on financial and economic issues, treasury, drawing up budgets and financial reports, invoicing third parties, administrating incoming invoices and (travel) declarations, and drafting outgoing invoices and (debit) collection. Introduction At TU/e, we believe that scientific excellence requires strong and reliable operations that are fit for purpose. Finance & Control plays a key role in this. With professionals working in both central and decentralized teams across the campus, the service department supports the Executive Board, departments, and services by providing financial insight, advice, and support closely aligned with their core processes. Through disciplines such as control, financial administration, project control, reporting & analysis, procurement, and business development, Finance & Control makes an essential contribution to the university’s ambitions. The societal and financial challenges facing universities require a Finance & Control organization that continuously strengthens its professionalism, effectiveness, efficiency and strategic impact. The department Finance & Control has the assignment to make strong and impactful steps in the coming years regarding its operational excellence, service delivery, control, compliance and productivity/efficiency. That is why we are seeking a Director Finance & Control who serves as a strong partner to the Executive Board while also working together with the organization to further strengthen the services, collaboration, and strategic impact of Finance & Control. Someone who, with vision, trust, and decisiveness, and attention for people management, contributes to an organization that is of great value to TU/e. Are you an experienced financial leader ready to take on a challenging role with significant strategic and organizational impact? If so, we'd love to hear from you. Job Description The Director Finance & Control is ultimately responsible for the functioning of the service department and therefore for the development of the financial strategy and policy and for the finance operations. You manage the six-member management team of the service department, and report to the portfolio holder in the Executive Board with a functional line to the audit committee of the Supervisory Board. In addition to ensuring the continuity and quality of the financial function, a key part of the role is to lead a significant professionalization and improvement agenda within the Finance & Control organization. The department is tasked with making substantial progress in strengthening operational excellence, standardizing and simplifying core processes, increasing productivity and effectiveness, improving service delivery to internal stakeholders, and fostering a culture of ownership, accountability, and continuous improvement. The Director Finance & Control will play a pivotal role in shaping and delivering this transformation together with the management team and the wider organization. Success in this role requires a leader who combines courage and decisiveness with empathy and authenticity. Someone who creates clarity and accountability, encourages open dialogue, builds trust, and inspires people to contribute to a shared ambition. You work closely with the Executive Board, the deans and directors of business operations of the departments, and the directors of your fellow support service departments. In addition, you maintain contact with the various (research) institutes, special programs and joint ventures and, as director of Finance & Control of the TU/e group, you also have a collaborative role with TU/e Participations BV, which includes 60 participations. Naturally, you play an important role in the relationship with banks and accountants. Furthermore, you maintain a network with other regional and national (collaboration) partners and you have an important role in the representation of TU/e in national partnerships such as ‘Universiteiten van Nederland’(UNL). In order to finance the university’s continued growth and the intended extensive programs in areas such as ICT and campus development, the investment task for the coming years will be a point of attention in the short term. The Finance & Control service department plays a prominent and active role in this regard. The Beethoven program requires specific attention with a key role for Finance & Control and its director when it comes, among other things, to (financial) substantiation and collaboration in the Brainport context and with the government. In summary, the new Director Finance & Control will play a key role in supporting TU/e's ambitions while leading a significant transformation and professionalization agenda within the Finance & Control organization. We are looking for a leader who combines strategic financial expertise with a proven ability to lead organizational change, bringing people together around a shared ambition and successfully translating change ambitions into tangible improvements. The ideal candidate creates clarity and trust, fosters ownership, collaboration and engagement, and has the courage and decisiveness to deliver lasting impact. Job Requirements You have extensive experience in leading the financial function - strategy, policy and operations - in a large and complex public or semi-public organization, preferably in a knowledge-intensive environment with highly educated professionals. You have in-depth knowledge of financial management, planning and control, financial reporting, and risk management. Preferably you have led multiple complex change projects in different organizations and understand and appreciate the dynamics in changing environments. Naturally you have a university degree in business economics or business administration, complemented with accountancy/risk and compliance education. Your mastery of Dutch and English is at C1 level in both speech and writing. You are a strong leader with natural authority and you know how to activate both employees and management. You have an excellent antenna for mutual relationships and interests, and you are diplomatic. At the same time, your focus is on driving results and you foster a culture of holding each other accountable. You can advise a board at a strategic level, transcending the financial position, in a solicited and unsolicited manner. You do this in a unifying manner and have authority. You explicitly seek out collaboration with your fellow service department directors, the deans and the directors of business operations of the departments for whom you are the figurehead and point of contact for the service, authoritatively fulfilling the role of advisor and sparring partner. You are able to translate financial topics in a comprehensible manner according to the (needs of the) broad and more generalized administrative layers of the organization. Conditions of Employment An exciting position within an international yet personal university. You are right in the middle of the students, on a green campus within walking distance of the central station. Besides beautiful architecture, you will find varied workplaces and excellent sports facilities. We also offer you: Salary in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities , scale 16, ranging from €8.309,- to €10.815,- gross base salary per month (full-time), depending on your knowledge and experience. In addition to your base salary, you will receive an 8% holiday allowance and an 8.3% year-end bonus, both calculated based on your annual gross base salary. Generous leave options: a standard 29 days (based on a 38 hour working week) per year that you can increase to 41 days by working two hours more per week (flexible working hours). This is prorated if you work part-time. As a TU/e employee, you participate in the ABP pension scheme, providing retirement pension and pension benefits for surviving dependents and occupational disability. TU/e pays 70% of the pension premium, while employees contribute the remaining 30%. A favorable arrangement for more holidays or a sabbatical. A selection model for additional fringe benefits. Working hours in consultation for an optimal work-life balance. Unlimited access to the modern on‑campus TU/e Student Sports Center at an exceptionally affordable rate. We support your wellbeing with free 24/7 access to OpenUp, providing you and your family with mental health support, expert guidance, and online training. Scope for your talent with advancement prospects and excellent development opportunities such as mentoring, workshops and coaching. Partially paid parental leave and reimbursement for commuting expenses, working from home and the internet. On our website you can discover even more information about our conditions of employment . Build on your career at TU/e! About us We are a leading international university where scientific curiosity meets a hands-on mindset. We work in an open and collaborative way with high-tech industries to tackle complex societal challenges. Our responsible and respectful approach ensures impact — today and in the future. TU/e is home to over 13,000 students and more than 7,000 staff, forming a diverse and vibrant academic community. Discover what Light Up means to TU/e in our short company video . Our university is located in Brainport Eindhoven — a world‑leading tech region with more than 7,000 high‑tech companies and strong R&D activity. Known for breakthroughs in AI, photonics, semiconductors and advanced manufacturing, Brainport is a place where technology serves people and society. Learn more about the Brainport region here . In January 2026, we launched the vision and strategy for TU/e Operations, setting a clear ambition: to become the most personal, connected, and seamless university operations in the Netherlands by 2035. This strategy describes the direction in which our operations should develop across the university. The core competences are focused, efficient, effective, co-creative. This entails a one TU/e approach in which cross departmental operations are delivered in a collaborative and harmonized approach. Information Visit our website for more information about the application process . You can also contact Rob van der Linden, Senior Recruiter - r.m.e.v.d.linden@ remove-this. tue.nl or +31 6 39582273 Are you inspired and would like to know more about working at TU/e? Please visit our career page. Application If you are interested, please use the ‘apply’ button to send us your CV and letter of application with your motivation and a description of your qualifications. Ensure that you submit all the requested application documents. We give priority to complete applications. The application process may also include an assessment and a request for references. Screening of candidates begins as soon as applications are received and continues until the position is filled. Where applicable, internal candidates will be given priority over external candidates where they are equally suitable. We look forward to receiving your application! Please note You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. A pre-employment screening (e.g. knowledge security check) can be part of the selection procedure. For more information on the knowledge security check, please consult the National Knowledge Security Guidelines . Important for non-EU applicants: Please be aware that for this position, specific residence permit requirements apply. If you are a non-EU national, you may not be eligible to legally work in this role under current Dutch immigration regulations. We strongly advise you to contact our Staff Immigration Team ( staffimmigration@ remove-this. tue.nl ) before applying to check your eligibility and to receive further guidance. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Reference number: 2026/654 Apply now Share this vacancy Share Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Why join TU/e? Join the Eindhoven University of Technology and its thriving community of scientists, students, and professionals. Shape your own career as you become part of a personal university with a big impact. A university where students and lecturers know each other on a first-name basis and work together on innovative projects with real-life significance. Why TU/e? Excellent fundamental research combined with a hands-on mentality Explore our research State-of-the-art research labs Explore our labs World-leading university in cooperation with industry Explore our ecosystem Bachelor programs Master programs Admission and enrollment Working at TU/e Search staff Route & map Education Guide Intranet Cursor Navigation address De Zaale Eindhoven Phone number: +31 (0)40 247 9111 Contact Postal address PO Box 513 5600 MB Eindhoven Follow us Like TU/e on Facebook Follow TU/e on LinkedIn Follow TU/e on YouTube © 2026 TU/e Disclaimer Privacy Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor Education Education Education Why study at TU/e Bachelor College Graduate School Become a TU/e student Academy for Learning and Teaching TU/e innovation Space Professional Education Research Research Research Institutes Research Areas Research Groups Research Labs Research Projects Researchers Departments Grants & Awards Research Support Our university Our university Our university About the University Departments Calendar and events TU/e Campus Library Community Student Teams Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Support Staff PhD EngD At TU/e News and Events News and Events News and Events News overview Media relations Impact Impact Impact Cooperation with Industry Knowledge Transfer Office TU/e Participations Starting your business Intellectual Property Stay rates Brainport for Eachother TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor"
