2_BODY_PURPOSES_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PURPOSES#] [#IABV2_LABEL_FEATURES#] [#IABV2_BODY_FEATURES_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_FEATURES#] [#IABV2_LABEL_PARTNERS#] [#IABV2_BODY_PARTNERS_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PARTNERS#] About Cookies are small text files that can be used by websites to make a user's experience more efficient. The law states that we can store cookies on your device if they are strictly necessary for the operation of this site. For all other types of cookies we need your permission. This website uses different types of cookies. Some cookies are placed by third party services that appear on our pages. You can at any time change or withdraw your consent from the cookie declaration on our website. Please state your consent ID and date when you contact us regarding your consent. For more information about the use of cookies at TU/e you can visit: https://www.tue.nl/en/storage/disclaimer Do not sell or share my personal information Deny Allow selection Customize Allow all Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact × search Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies PhD on Ultracold ele... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies PhD on Ultracold electron source development for time-resolved protein crystallography Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: PhD Organisation: Department of Applied Physics and Science Education Apply no later than: 21-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 3.204 - € 4.051 Apply now Introduction Are you excited to solve technical challenges with a real-world application? Are you eager to build something truly unique in the world? Job Description Development of a pulsed electron source with extreme transverse bunch brightness, based on photo-ionization of laser-cooled atoms, for time-resolved protein crystallography. Context: ERC-funded project “Cool T-ReX” Goal: Develop a unique and innovative instrument to enable time-resolved protein crystallography with electrons (and be the first in the world in doing so). Scientific relevance: Understanding how proteins function is crucial to improving medicine and unraveling processes that are fundamental to life. Time-resolved protein crystallography uniquely allows following the conformational change of a protein with unprecedented spatial and temporal resolution, yielding a “molecular movie” of how the protein performs its function. This is currently only possible on large-scale X-ray facilities. In this project we will build the very first instrument that can make such movies through time-resolved protein crystallography with electrons rather than X-rays, on a laboratory-scale setup. Next, through collaboration with leading research groups in time-resolved protein crystallography, we will demonstrate the instrument’s capabilities in time-resolved crystallography experiments on photo-active proteins with medical relevance (and used in the field of optogenetics, awarded this year’s Nobel Prize in Medicine!). Your role: Drive the development of this unique instrument. You will build on our research group’s two decades of experience in building electron sources based on the photo-ionization of laser-cooled atoms. This technique has demonstrated electron pulses with record-low transverse temperatures, corresponding to a high transverse coherence, as needed for protein crystallography. In this project we will push this transverse coherence even further, making use of some of the unique capabilities of this source technology. The result will be an electron beam with a “transverse bunch brightness” that is three orders of magnitude beyond the current state of the art. To reach this ambitious goal, you will work with a team of experienced technicians, a second PhD student, a PostDoc, and the PI (Julius Huijts). We are part of the larger Coherence and Quantum Technology group in the Department of Applied Physics. Job Requirements A MSc degree in Applied Physics, Engineering Physics, Mechatronics with a strong physics component, or similar. You can work in a team, are open to new ideas, can communicate with people outside your own field. You take initiative, are able to organize your own work load. You have an affinity with the goal of this project. You have a background or a proven affinity with at least two of the following (please highlight this in your application): o  Mechanical and optical design o  Complex optical setups o  Charged particle optics o  Cold atoms o  High vacuum o  High voltage Fluent in spoken and written English (C1 level). A research-oriented attitude Conditions of Employment A meaningful job in a dynamic and ambitious university, in an interdisciplinary setting and within an international network. You will work on a beautiful, green campus within walking distance of the central train station. In addition, we offer you: Full-time employment for four years, with an intermediate assessment after nine months. You will spend a minimum of 10% of your four-year employment on teaching tasks, with a maximum of 15% per year of your employment. Starting date is somewhat flexible, but ideally Feb 1 2027. Salary and benefits (such as a pension scheme, paid pregnancy and maternity leave, partially paid parental leave) in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities , scale P (min. € 3,204 - max. € 4,051 gross base salary per month (full-time)). In addition to your base salary, you will receive an 8% holiday allowance and an "
    },
    "https://www.tue.nl/en/working-at-tue/vacancy-overview/postdoc-in-experimental-photonic-quantum-computing": {
      "title": "PostDoc in experimental photonic quantum computing",
      "description": "PostDoc in experimental photonic quantum computing Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies PostDoc in experimen... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies PostDoc in experimental photonic quantum computing Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Postdoctorate Organisation: Department of Applied Physics and Science Education Apply no later than: 19-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.422 - € 5.760 Apply now Introduction Are you eager to work on the next generation of quantum computing devices? Job Description Quantum computing has the potential to revolutionize information processing, by unlocking new capabilities in chemistry, medicine, AI, and cryptography. As quantum computing continues to mature, the need to make scalable, reliable components belong paramount. Photonic quantum computing has an advantage here because of strong technological overlap with the already well-established photonics industry. In this project, we will design, construct and test a prototype resource state generation module for use in a photonic quantum computer. Such a resource state generator takes single photons, entangles them in through linear optics plus partial measurement, converting the single photons into a collective quantum state which can be further processed by the rest of the computer. The specific goal here is to integrate (potentially heterogeneously) the various components of this system on a single chip, coming to an individual prototype module that can be tested to infer design parameters of the overall quantum computer. This project is part of the larger photonic quantum computing mission on Photon Delta. Photon Delta represents the photonics ecosystem in the Netherlands. The quantum computing mission brings together a variety of industrial and academic partners to advance photonic quantum computing in the Netherlands and is led by QuiX Quantum. You will contribute to the activities of the quantum photonic information processing (QPIP) team, which is embedded in the Coherence and Quantum Technology group, and in the Photonic Integration group. These groups have strong industrial links to both the quantum and the photonics industry through their spinouts and projects. QPIP is a young team; there is both the opportunity and the expectation to help shape the growth and culture of the team. Job Requirements Motivated researcher, with a PhD in integrated photonics, quantum technologies or a related domain. Expertise in both integrated photonics and quantum technologies Ability to conduct high quality academic research, reflected in demonstratable outputs. A team player who enjoys coaching PhD and Master's students and working in a dynamic, interdisciplinary team. A proven ability to manage complex projects to completion on schedule. Excellent (written and verbal) proficiency in English, good communication and leadership skills. Conditions of Employment A meaningful job in a dynamic and ambitious university, in an interdisciplinary setting and within an international network. You will work on a beautiful, green campus within walking distance of the central train station. In addition, we offer you: Full-time employment for 1,5 years, with the possibility of an extension. Salary in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities , scale 10, ranging from € 4,422 (step 4) to € 5,760 gross base salary per month (full-time). In addition to your base salary, you will receive an 8% holiday allowance and an 8.3% year-end bonus, both calculated based on your annual gross base salary. Generous leave options: a standard 29 days (based on a 38 hour working week) per year that you can increase to 41 days by working two hours more per week (flexible working hours). This is prorated if you work part-time. As a TU/e employee, you participate in the ABP pension scheme, providing retirement pension and pension benefits for surviving dependents and occupational disability. TU/e pays 70% of the pension premium, while employees contribute the remaining 30%. High-quality training programs on general skills, didactics and topics related to research and valorization. An excellent technical infrastructure, and on-campus children's day care. Unlimited access to the modern on‑campus TU/e Student Sports Center at an exceptionally affordable rate. We support your wellbeing with free 24/7 access to OpenUp, providing you and your family with mental health support, expert guidance, and online training. Partially paid parental leave and an allowance for commuting, working from home and internet costs. A TU/e Postdoc Association that helps you to build a stronger and broader academic and personal network, and offers tailored support, training and workshops. A Staff Immigration Team is available for international candidates, as are a tax compensation scheme (the Expat Scheme ) and a compensation for moving expenses. On our website you can discover even more information about our conditions of employment . Build on your career at TU/e! About us We are a leading international university where scientific curiosity meets a hands-on mindset. We work in an open and collaborative way with high-tech industries to tackle complex societal challenges. Our responsible and respectful approach ensures impact — today and in the future. TU/e is home to over 13,000 students and more than 7,000 staff, forming a diverse and vibrant academic community. Discover what Light Up means to TU/e in our short company video . Our university is located in Brainport Eindhoven — a world‑leading tech region with more than 7,000 high‑tech companies and strong R&D activity. Known for breakthroughs in AI, photonics, semiconductors and advanced manufacturing, Brainport is a place where technology serves people and society. Learn more about the Brainport region here . The Department of Applied Physics and Science Education is a research-driven department housing high-quality educational programs, all featuring strong connections between research and education. Our research is clustered in three focal areas: Fluids, Bio and Soft Matter (FBSM); Plasmas and Beams (PB); and Nano, Quantum and Photonics (NQP). Our shared ambition is to equip the next generation of ‘engineers of the future’ with the knowledge and the skills they will need to impact science, innovation, and society, from regional to global scales. Information Do you recognize yourself in this profile and would you like to know more? Please contact the hiring manager Dr. Jelmer Renema, Associate Professor, j.j.renema@ remove-this. tue.nl . Visit our website for more information about the application process . You can also contact HRServices.apse@ remove-this. tue.nl . Are you inspired and would like to know more about working at TU/e? Please visit our career page. Application We invite you to submit a complete application using the apply-button. The application should include a: Cover letter in which you describe your motivation and qualifications for the position. Curriculum vitae, including a list of your publications and the contact information of three references. Kindly note that we may reach out to references at any stage of the recruitment process. We recommend notifying your references upon submitting your application. List of up to five self-selected ‘best publications’. Ensure that you submit all the requested application documents. Please note that incomplete applications may not be considered and could be rejected. We look forward to receiving your application and will screen it as soon as possible. The vacancy will remain open until the position is filled. Please note You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. A pre-employment screening (e.g. knowledge security check) can be part of the selection procedure. For more information on the knowledge security check, please consult the National Knowledge Security Guidelines . Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Reference number: 2026/653 Apply now Share this vacancy Share Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Related vacancies Postdoc In Algebraic Graph Theory and Applications Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Postdoctorate Organisation: Department of Mathematics and Computer Science Apply no later than: 31-12-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.422 - € 5.760 Read more PostDoc on Targeted Proteomics for Protein Biomarker Standardization Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Postdoctorate Organisation: Department of Biomedical Engineering Apply no later than: 05-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.422 - € 5.760 Read more Postdoc on Real-Time EMT Modelling of Future MV/LV Distribution Systems (UTOPYS) Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Postdoctorate Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 14-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.422 - € 5.760 Read more Why join TU/e? Join the Eindhoven University of Technology and its thriving community of scientists, students, and professionals. Shape your own career as you become part of a personal university with a big impact. A university where students and lecturers know each other on a first-name basis and work together on innovative projects with real-life significance. Why TU/e? Excellent fundamental research combined with a hands-on mentality Explore our research State-of-the-art research labs Explore our labs World-leading university in cooperation with industry Explore our ecosystem Bachelor programs Master programs Admission and enrollment Working at TU/e Search staff Route & map Education Guide Intranet Cursor Navigation address De Zaale Eindhoven Phone number: +31 (0)40 247 9111 Contact Postal address PO Box 513 5600 MB Eindhoven Follow us Like TU/e on Facebook Follow TU/e on LinkedIn Follow TU/e on YouTube © 2026 TU/e Disclaimer Privacy Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor Education Education Education Why study at TU/e Bachelor College Graduate School Become a TU/e student Academy for Learning and Teaching TU/e innovation Space Professional Education Research Research Research Institutes Research Areas Research Groups Research Labs Research Projects Researchers Departments Grants & Awards Research Support Our university Our university Our university About the University Departments Calendar and events TU/e Campus Library Community Student Teams Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Support Staff PhD EngD At TU/e News and Events News and Events News and Events News overview Media relations Impact Impact Impact Cooperation with Industry Knowledge Transfer Office TU/e Participations Starting your business Intellectual Property Stay rates Brainport for Eachother TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor"
    },
    "https://www.tue.nl/en/working-at-tue/vacancy-overview/postdoc-in-quantum-computing-architecture": {
      "title": "Postdoc in quantum computing architecture",
      "description": "Postdoc in quantum computing architecture Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies Postdoc in quantum c... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies Postdoc in quantum computing architecture Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Postdoctorate Organisation: Department of Applied Physics and Science Education Apply no later than: 19-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.422 - € 5.760 Apply now Introduction Are you eager to design the computing architecture of tomorrow? Job Description Quantum computing has the potential to revolutionize information processing, by unlocking new capabilities in chemistry, medicine, AI, and cryptography. As quantum computing continues to mature, scaling becomes an important consideration. Because of this, the overall architecture of large scale quantum computing systems is coming into focus as a central research question in the field. In this project, we will work on the design of an architecture for large scale photonic quantum computing, with a focus on incorporating our recent results on non-deterministic error-reducing photonic circuits into the architecture. Using such a circuit, we recently demonstrated experimentally the first below-threshold results in photonics. The goal here is to apply this idea to the larger architecture of the full photonic quantum computer. This project is part of the larger photonic quantum computing mission on Photon Delta. Photon Delta represents the photonics ecosystem in the Netherlands. The quantum computing mission brings together a variety of industrial and academic partners to advance photonic quantum computing in the Netherlands and is led by QuiX Quantum. You will contribute to the activities of the quantum photonic information processing (QPIP) team, which is embedded in the Coherence and Quantum Technology group, and in the Photonic Integration group. These groups have strong industrial links to both the quantum and the photonics industry through their spinouts and projects. QPIP is a young team; there is both the opportunity and the expectation to help shape the growth and culture of the team. Job Requirements Motivated researcher, with a PhD in quantum computing or quantum information. Expertise in photonic quantum computing and/or error correction (in any modality) is a plus. Ability to conduct high quality academic research, reflected in demonstratable outputs. A team player who enjoys coaching PhD and Master's students and working in a dynamic, interdisciplinary team. A proven ability to manage complex projects to completion on schedule. Excellent (written and verbal) proficiency in English, good communication and leadership skills. Conditions of Employment A meaningful job in a dynamic and ambitious university, in an interdisciplinary setting and within an international network. You will work on a beautiful, green campus within walking distance of the central train station. In addition, we offer you: Full-time employment for 1,5 years, with the possibility of an extension. Salary in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities , scale 10, ranging from € 4,422 (step 4) to € 5,760 gross base salary per month (full-time). In addition to your base salary, you will receive an 8% holiday allowance and an 8.3% year-end bonus, both calculated based on your annual gross base salary. Generous leave options: a standard 29 days (based on a 38 hour working week) per year that you can increase to 41 days by working two hours more per week (flexible working hours). This is prorated if you work part-time. As a TU/e employee, you participate in the ABP pension scheme, providing retirement pension and pension benefits for surviving dependents and occupational disability. TU/e pays 70% of the pension premium, while employees contribute the remaining 30%. High-quality training programs on general skills, didactics and topics related to research and valorization. An excellent technical infrastructure, and on-campus children's day care. Unlimited access to the modern on‑campus TU/e Student Sports Center at an exceptionally affordable rate. We support your wellbeing with free 24/7 access to OpenUp, providing you and your family with mental health support, expert guidance, and online training. Partially paid parental leave and an allowance for commuting, working from home and internet costs. A TU/e Postdoc Association that helps you to build a stronger and broader academic and personal network, and offers tailored support, training and workshops. A Staff Immigration Team is available for international candidates, as are a tax compensation scheme (the Expat Scheme ) and a compensation for moving expenses. On our website you can discover even more information about our conditions of employment . Build on your career at TU/e! About us We are a leading international university where scientific curiosity meets a hands-on mindset. We work in an open and collaborative way with high-tech industries to tackle complex societal challenges. Our responsible and respectful approach ensures impact — today and in the future. TU/e is home to over 13,000 students and more than 7,000 staff, forming a diverse and vibrant academic community. Discover what Light Up means to TU/e in our short company video . Our university is located in Brainport Eindhoven — a world‑leading tech region with more than 7,000 high‑tech companies and strong R&D activity. Known for breakthroughs in AI, photonics, semiconductors and advanced manufacturing, Brainport is a place where technology serves people and society. Learn more about the Brainport region here . The Department of Applied Physics and Science Education is a research-driven department housing high-quality educational programs, all featuring strong connections between research and education. Our research is clustered in three focal areas: Fluids, Bio and Soft Matter (FBSM); Plasmas and Beams (PB); and Nano, Quantum and Photonics (NQP). Our shared ambition is to equip the next generation of ‘engineers of the future’ with the knowledge and the skills they will need to impact science, innovation, and society, from regional to global scales. Information Do you recognize yourself in this profile and would you like to know more? Please contact the hiring manager Dr. Jelmer Renema, Associate Professor, j.j.renema@ remove-this. tue.nl . Visit our website for more information about the application process . You can also contact HRServices.apse@ remove-this. tue.nl . Are you inspired and would like to know more about working at TU/e? Please visit our career page. Application We invite you to submit a complete application using the apply-button. The application should include a: Cover letter in which you describe your motivation and qualifications for the position. Curriculum vitae, including a list of your publications and the contact information of three references. Kindly note that we may reach out to references at any stage of the recruitment process. We recommend notifying your references upon submitting your application. List of up to five self-selected ‘best publications’. Ensure that you submit all the requested application documents. Please note that incomplete applications may not be considered and could be rejected. We look forward to receiving your application and will screen it as soon as possible. The vacancy will remain open until the position is filled. Please note You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. A pre-employment screening (e.g. knowledge security check) can be part of the selection procedure. For more information on the knowledge security check, please consult the National Knowledge Security Guidelines . Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Reference number: 2026/655 Apply now Share this vacancy Share Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Related vacancies Postdoc In Algebraic Graph Theory and Applications Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Postdoctorate Organisation: Department of Mathematics and Computer Science Apply no later than: 31-12-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.422 - € 5.760 Read more PostDoc on Targeted Proteomics for Protein Biomarker Standardization Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Postdoctorate Organisation: Department of Biomedical Engineering Apply no later than: 05-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.422 - € 5.760 Read more Postdoc on Real-Time EMT Modelling of Future MV/LV Distribution Systems (UTOPYS) Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Postdoctorate Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 14-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.422 - € 5.760 Read more Why join TU/e? Join the Eindhoven University of Technology and its thriving community of scientists, students, and professionals. Shape your own career as you become part of a personal university with a big impact. A university where students and lecturers know each other on a first-name basis and work together on innovative projects with real-life significance. Why TU/e? Excellent fundamental research combined with a hands-on mentality Explore our research State-of-the-art research labs Explore our labs World-leading university in cooperation with industry Explore our ecosystem Bachelor programs Master programs Admission and enrollment Working at TU/e Search staff Route & map Education Guide Intranet Cursor Navigation address De Zaale Eindhoven Phone number: +31 (0)40 247 9111 Contact Postal address PO Box 513 5600 MB Eindhoven Follow us Like TU/e on Facebook Follow TU/e on LinkedIn Follow TU/e on YouTube © 2026 TU/e Disclaimer Privacy Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor Education Education Education Why study at TU/e Bachelor College Graduate School Become a TU/e student Academy for Learning and Teaching TU/e innovation Space Professional Education Research Research Research Institutes Research Areas Research Groups Research Labs Research Projects Researchers Departments Grants & Awards Research Support Our university Our university Our university About the University Departments Calendar and events TU/e Campus Library Community Student Teams Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Support Staff PhD EngD At TU/e News and Events News and Events News and Events News overview Media relations Impact Impact Impact Cooperation with Industry Knowledge Transfer Office TU/e Participations Starting your business Intellectual Property Stay rates Brainport for Eachother TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor"
