 Type : HTML Local Storage YtIdbMeta#databases [x2] Used to track user’s interaction with embedded content. Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : IndexedDB __Secure-ROLLOUT_TOKEN Used to track user’s interaction with embedded content. Maximum Storage Duration : 180 days Type : HTTP Cookie __Secure-YEC Stores the user's video player preferences using embedded YouTube video Maximum Storage Duration : Session Type : HTTP Cookie __Secure-YNID Used to track user’s interaction with embedded content. Maximum Storage Duration : 180 days Type : HTTP Cookie LogsDatabaseV2:V#||LogsRequestsStore Used to track user’s interaction with embedded content. Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : IndexedDB VISITOR_INFO1_LIVE Tries to estimate the users' bandwidth on pages with integrated YouTube videos. Maximum Storage Duration : 180 days Type : HTTP Cookie YSC Registers a unique ID to keep statistics of what videos from YouTube the user has seen. Maximum Storage Duration : Session Type : HTTP Cookie Unclassified 4 Unclassified cookies are cookies that we are in the process of classifying, together with the providers of individual cookies. LinkedIn 1 Learn more about this provider li_fat_id Pending Maximum Storage Duration : 30 days Type : HTTP Cookie Tu/e 2 Learn more about this provider aff_93e95bd6a Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Session Type : HTTP Cookie page_view_count Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Session Type : HTML Local Storage YouTube 1 Learn more about this provider yt-player-caption-persistence Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : HTML Local Storage Cross-domain consent [#BULK_CONSENT_DOMAINS_COUNT#] [#BULK_CONSENT_TITLE#] List of domains your consent applies to: [#BULK_CONSENT_DOMAINS#] Cookie declaration last updated on 9/27/26 by Cookiebot [#IABV2_TITLE#] [#IABV2_BODY_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_LEGITIMATE_INTEREST_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PREFERENCE_INTRO#] [#IABV2_LABEL_PURPOSES#] [#IABV2_BODY_PURPOSES_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PURPOSES#] [#IABV2_LABEL_FEATURES#] [#IABV2_BODY_FEATURES_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_FEATURES#] [#IABV2_LABEL_PARTNERS#] [#IABV2_BODY_PARTNERS_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PARTNERS#] About Cookies are small text files that can be used by websites to make a user's experience more efficient. The law states that we can store cookies on your device if they are strictly necessary for the operation of this site. For all other types of cookies we need your permission. This website uses different types of cookies. Some cookies are placed by third party services that appear on our pages. You can at any time change or withdraw your consent from the cookie declaration on our website. Please state your consent ID and date when you contact us regarding your consent. For more information about the use of cookies at TU/e you can visit: https://www.tue.nl/en/storage/disclaimer Do not sell or share my personal information Deny Allow selection Customize Allow all Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact × search Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies Functional Manager e... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies Functional Manager exam systems Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: IT Organisation: Library and Information Services Apply no later than: 20-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 3.873 - € 5.760 Apply now Societal challenges demand new knowledge. It is the task of the TU/e to develop this knowledge by adapting and changing research and education. At Library and Information Services (LIS) we look ahead, together with our scientists and students, and constantly provide the best possible library and information services to enable the creation of this new knowledge. Introduction Are you an enthusiastic and curious professional with a passion for education? We are looking for you! At the TU/e, scientists and students continuously create the unthinkable. The strength of the IT landscape is their key to success and, hence, so are you. These creative minds expect you to offer them a solution for tomorrow that doesn’t exist today. Together we are building the high-performance backbone that this epicenter of science and technology demands. Job Description Do you want to contribute to the quality of our education by further professionalizing the exam organization? As a functional manager for exam systems, you collaborate closely with education and other IT/IV teams to ensure a stable and scalable exam process. Together, we make secure and flexible examination possible for the entire university. About the team You will be part of the Assessment Support team within the Education Area of Library & Information Services (LIS). The team is part of the IT service department, but you will also work very closely with educational (service) departments and colleagues. The goal of Assessment Support is to translate all needs in the field of examination into working digital solutions. This means that you will not only manage systems, but also actively support the design and development of exam processes. The team manages several systems that are part of the overall exam chain: 2 exam systems for creating and taking digital and on-paper exams; 2 systems for securing student laptops during digital exams; And 1 proctoring system to facilitate students that take an exam abroad. These systems are integrated and require careful management and cooperation with many different stakeholders. What you will do As a functional manager, you play a crucial role in maintaining and professionalizing exam systems & processes, and ensuring its continuity. You make an important contribution to a future-proof and scalable exam chain. As part of the assessment support team, you will: Assess, test and supervise changes and releases of the exam systems Ensure stable and scalable operation of exam systems Develop and maintain golden images for exams in Azure AVD Solve issues with Azure AVD during exams Take the lead in collaboration with end users, support staff and suppliers Standardize and optimize exam processes, even when things are unclear Contribute to the further growth and adoption of new exam formats within TU/e What a day could look like You start your day with coffee and a catch-up with colleagues before investigating an exam incident from Friday. After discussing your findings during the Daily Scrum, you wrap up the investigation and update the exam coordinator. The rest of the morning is spent testing keyboard layouts to solve issues caused by foreign keyboards. After a lunchtime walk across the campus and a quick check at an exam location, you return to review system release notes and assess their impact. A short call with a lecturer helps clarify part of the grading process. You finish the day by sharing your concerns with a supplier, setting the stage for follow-up actions tomorrow. Job Requirements Does this job description make you heart beat faster? Then we would like to receive your application, especially if you recognize yourself in the following characteristics: HBO/WO work and thinking level 3+ years of experience in a technical and/or educational work environment Professional written and spoken communication skills in Dutch and English Proactive and pragmatic work attitude, both independently and in a team Proven ability to easily master new technology You are able to provide independent advice and substantiate your choices You are capable of weighing up inte"
    },
