umber of times that they are shown the same advertisement. Maximum Storage Duration : 1 day Type : HTTP Cookie _uetvid Used to track visitors on multiple websites, in order to present relevant advertisement based on the visitor's preferences. Maximum Storage Duration : 1 year Type : HTTP Cookie Spotify 2 Learn more about this provider sp_landing Used to implement audio-content from Spotify on the website. Can also be used to register user interaction and preferences in context with audio-content - This can serve statistics and marketing purposes. Maximum Storage Duration : 1 day Type : HTTP Cookie sp_t Used to implement audio-content from Spotify on the website. Can also be used to register user interaction and preferences in context with audio-content - This can serve statistics and marketing purposes. Maximum Storage Duration : 1 year Type : HTTP Cookie Unibuddy 3 Learn more about this provider __mpq_#_# Collects data on user behaviour and interaction in order to optimize the website and make advertisement on the website more relevant. Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : HTML Local Storage mp_#_mixpanel Pending Maximum Storage Duration : 1 year Type : HTTP Cookie ServiceWorkerLogsDatabase#SWHealthLog Necessary for the implementation and functionality of YouTube video-content on the website. Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : IndexedDB YouTube 16 Learn more about this provider LAST_RESULT_ENTRY_KEY [x2] Used to track user’s interaction with embedded content. Maximum Storage Duration : Session Type : HTTP Cookie TESTCOOKIESENABLED [x2] Used to track user’s interaction with embedded content. Maximum Storage Duration : 1 day Type : HTTP Cookie yt-icons-last-purged [x2] Necessary for the implementation and functionality of YouTube video-content on the website. Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : HTML Local Storage ytidb::LAST_RESULT_ENTRY_KEY [x2] Used to track user’s interaction with embedded content. Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : HTML Local Storage YtIdbMeta#databases [x2] Used to track user’s interaction with embedded content. Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : IndexedDB __Secure-ROLLOUT_TOKEN Used to track user’s interaction with embedded content. Maximum Storage Duration : 180 days Type : HTTP Cookie __Secure-YEC Stores the user's video player preferences using embedded YouTube video Maximum Storage Duration : Session Type : HTTP Cookie __Secure-YNID Used to track user’s interaction with embedded content. Maximum Storage Duration : 180 days Type : HTTP Cookie LogsDatabaseV2:V#||LogsRequestsStore Used to track user’s interaction with embedded content. Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : IndexedDB VISITOR_INFO1_LIVE Tries to estimate the users' bandwidth on pages with integrated YouTube videos. Maximum Storage Duration : 180 days Type : HTTP Cookie YSC Registers a unique ID to keep statistics of what videos from YouTube the user has seen. Maximum Storage Duration : Session Type : HTTP Cookie Unclassified 4 Unclassified cookies are cookies that we are in the process of classifying, together with the providers of individual cookies. LinkedIn 1 Learn more about this provider li_fat_id Pending Maximum Storage Duration : 30 days Type : HTTP Cookie Tu/e 2 Learn more about this provider aff_93e95bd6a Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Session Type : HTTP Cookie page_view_count Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Session Type : HTML Local Storage YouTube 1 Learn more about this provider yt-player-caption-persistence Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : HTML Local Storage Cross-domain consent [#BULK_CONSENT_DOMAINS_COUNT#] [#BULK_CONSENT_TITLE#] List of domains your consent applies to: [#BULK_CONSENT_DOMAINS#] Cookie declaration last updated on 9/27/26 by Cookiebot [#IABV2_TITLE#] [#IABV2_BODY_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_LEGITIMATE_INTEREST_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PREFERENCE_INTRO#] [#IABV2_LABEL_PURPOSES#] [#IABV2_BODY_PURPOSES_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PURPOSES#] [#IABV2_LABEL_FEATURES#] [#IABV2_BODY_FEATURES_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_FEATURES#] [#IABV2_LABEL_PARTNERS#] [#IABV2_BODY_PARTNERS_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PARTNERS#] About Cookies are small text files that can be used by websites to make a user's experience more efficient. The law states that we can store cookies on your device if they are strictly necessary for the operation of this site. For all other types of cookies we need your permission. This website uses different types of cookies. Some cookies are placed by third party services that appear on our pages. You can at any time change or withdraw your consent from the cookie declaration on our website. Please state your consent ID and date when you contact us regarding your consent. For more information about the use of cookies at TU/e you can visit: https://www.tue.nl/en/storage/disclaimer Do not sell or share my personal information Deny Allow selection Customize Allow all Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact × search Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies Strategisch Vastgoed... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies Strategisch Vastgoed Adviseur Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: Policy and staff Organisation: Campus and Facilities Apply no later than: 19-11-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 5.932 - € 7.573 Apply now Introductie Werk jij graag op het snijvlak van strategie, recht, vastgoed en samenwerking met externe partners? In deze rol draag je bij aan complexe dossiers rondom de ontwikkeling en positionering van de TU/e-campus. Vanuit jouw juridische achtergrond help je belangen, afspraken, risico’s en verantwoordelijkheden scherp te krijgen en vertaal je deze naar heldere adviezen en voorstellen. Campus & Facilities beheert de volledige levenscyclus van het TU/e-vastgoed: van ontwikkeling tot onderhoud, van technische installaties tot infrastructuur en facilitaire dienstverlening. Op 75 hectare campus en ruim 350.000 m² aan gebouwen werk je in een omgeving die voortdurend in ontwikkeling is. Midden in Brainport Eindhoven werk je samen met engineers, onderzoekers en specialisten aan één gezamenlijk doel: een campus die uitnodigt tot presteren, ontmoeten en samenwerken. Binnen Campus & Facilities is Integrale Campus Strategie (ICS) verantwoordelijk voor de strategie, beleidsontwikkeling en inhoudelijke kaders voor vastgoed en facilitair. We werken vanuit een breed multidisciplinair team van technisch consultants, huisvestingsadviseurs en specialisten op het gebied van onder andere duurzaamheid, integrale veiligheid, mobiliteit en parkmanagement. Juist die combinatie van strategische, beleidsmatige en technische expertise stelt ons in staat om complexe campusvraagstukken integraal te benaderen. Functieomschrijving Als Strategisch Adviseur Vastgoed, Contracten & Externe Relaties ben jij binnen Integrale Campus Strategie de adviseur die bij complexe vraagstukken vanuit juridisch perspectief wordt aangehaakt. Je werkt op strategisch en tactisch niveau en helpt om verschillende belangen, juridische kaders en inhoudelijke vraagstukken met elkaar te verbinden. Je bent strategisch contactpersoon voor externe organisaties die op of direct rond de TU/e-campus actief zijn, zoals GE HealthCare, Fontys en Woonbedrijf. Daarnaast onderhoud je nauwe relaties met de gemeente en andere relevante partijen in de directe omgeving van de campus. Je overziet deze relaties in samenhang en behartigt daarbij de belangen van TU/e. Vanuit jouw juridische achtergrond adviseer je over uiteenlopende dossiers op het gebied van vastgoed, huisvesting, samenwerking en gebiedsontwikkeling. Je doorgrondt contractuele en juridische vraagstukken, stelt de juiste vragen en brengt risico’s, verantwoordelijkheden en consequenties in beeld. Waar specialistische kennis nodig is, bijvoorbeeld op het gebied van vastgoedrecht, omgevingsrecht of stikstof, schakel je gericht externe expertise in en zorg je ervoor dat deze goed aansluit op het bredere vraagstuk. Je bent betrokken bij de voorbereiding en begeleiding van onder meer huur- en verhuurvraagstukken, aan- en verkoop van vastgoed, erfpachtconstructies en samenwerkingsovereenkomsten. Je ondersteunt en begeleidt strategische onderhandelingen en adviseert over de juridische en bestuurlijke consequenties van mogelijke keuzes. Je bereidt voorstellen en adviezen voor richting het managementteam en het College van Bestuur. Het formele mandaat voor het aangaan van overeenkomsten en transacties ligt elders binnen de organisatie. Ook bij strategisch-planologische dossiers, zoals ruimtelijke ordening en stikstof, vervul je een coördinerende en adviserende rol. Je hoeft hierin niet zelf de inhoudelijke specialist te zijn. Je zorgt dat duidelijk is welke expertise nodig is, organiseert deze waar nodig extern en bewaakt dat de uitkomsten worden vertaald naar bruikbare adviezen en keuzes voor TU/e. Vanuit je verantwoordelijkheid voor de strategische relaties werk je nauw samen met parkmanagement. Parkmanagement verzorgt de dagelijkse uitvoering en onderhoudt het operationele contact met partijen op de campus, bijvoorbeeld over verrekeningen en praktische vraagstukken. Jij bewaakt de bredere relatie en zorgt ervoor dat strategische, contractuele en bestuurlijke onderwerpen op de juiste plek worden besproken. Binnen ICS werk je nauw samen met collega’s met verschillende inhoudelijke expertises. Je hoeft hun vakgebied niet over te nemen, maar bent juist "
    },
    "https://www.tue.nl/en/working-at-tue/vacancy-overview/assistant-professor-in-experimental-fluid-dynamics": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor In Experimental Fluid Dynamics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor In Experimental Fluid Dynamics Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies Assistant Professor ... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies Assistant Professor In Experimental Fluid Dynamics Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Assistant Professor Organisation: Department of Chemical Engineering and Chemistry Apply no later than: 09-12-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 6.682 Apply now Advance the frontiers of experimental fluid dynamics and contribute to the development of sustainable technologies for energy conversion, chemical manufacturing, and the circular economy. As an Assistant Professor at TU/e, you will have the opportunity to establish an independent research program develop innovative diagnostic tools, and collaborate with leading experts in transport phenomena and chemical engineering. Introduction The Department of Chemical Engineering and Chemistry at Eindhoven University of Technology (TU/e) is seeking an ambitious and innovative Assistant Professor in Experimental Fluid Dynamics to strengthen its internationally recognized research activities in transport phenomena and multiphase systems. This position offers a unique opportunity to develop an independent research line at the forefront of advanced flow diagnostics while collaborating with leading experimental and computational researchers in chemical engineering and related disciplines. You will join a vibrant and collaborative academic environment with access to state-of-the-art laboratory infrastructure, strong industrial partnerships, and excellent opportunities to establish an internationally visible research program. Job Description We are looking for an outstanding researcher to establish and lead an innovative experimental research program focused on the development and application of advanced measurement and imaging techniques for multiphase reactive flows. Research topics of interest include, but are not limited to: Multiphase flows and reactive transport phenomena. Flows in energy, sustainability, and circular process technologies. Transport processes in porous media. Process intensification and microfluidics. Advanced optical and non-invasive measurement techniques. Particular interest will be given to candidates with expertise in advanced diagnostics such as: Particle Image Velocimetry (PIV). Digital Image Analysis (DIA). Structured Laser Illumination Planar Imaging (SLIPI). Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI). Other innovative imaging and sensing technologies. The successful candidate will further strengthen TU/e’s internationally leading activities in transport phenomena by developing new experimental methodologies that provide unprecedented insights into complex reactive systems. The position offers unique opportunities to combine advanced diagnostics with emerging approaches such as machine learning, data science, operando measurements, digital twins, and autonomous experimentation. Close collaboration with researchers across Chemical Engineering and Chemistry, Mechanical Engineering , Applied Physics , Mathematics & Computer Science , and industrial partners is strongly encouraged. The successful candidate will: Develop an internationally recognized and externally funded research program. Supervise and mentor BSc, MSc, EngD, PhD candidates and postdoctoral researchers. Publish in leading international journals and contribute to the scientific community. Initiate and lead national and international research collaborations. Contribute to the department's educational program through teaching and curriculum development. Play an active role in strengthening the department's collaborative and inclusive culture. Job Requirements We are seeking candidates who bring scientific excellence, creativity, and a collaborative mindset. You have: A PhD in Chemical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Applied Physics, or a closely related discipline. Postdoctoral experience is considered an advantage. An experience-appropriate record of scientific achievement, as evidenced by high-quality publications, invited presentations, awards, patents, and/or successful grant acquisition. Demonstrated ability to conduct innovative and impactful academic research. A clear vision for developing an internationally recognized research program. A strong interest in teaching and in developing excellent educational skills. The ability to work effectively in interdisciplinary teams. Strong communication, leadership, and mentoring skills. Excellent written and verbal English communication skills. Conditions of Employment A meaningful job in a dynamic and ambitious university, in an interdisciplinary setting and within an international network. You will work on a beautiful, green campus within walking distance of the central train station. In addition, we offer you: Salary in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities , scale 11, ranging from €4925 to €6682 gross base salary per month (full-time , based on relevant experience and/or seniority). In addition to your base salary, you will receive an 8% holiday allowance and an 8.3% year-end bonus, both calculated based on your annual gross base salary. Generous leave options: a standard 29 days (based on a 38 hour working week) per year that you can increase to 41 days by working two hours more per week (flexible working hours). This is prorated if you work part-time. As a TU/e employee, you participate in the ABP pension scheme, providing retirement pension and pension benefits for surviving dependents and occupational disability. TU/e pays 70% of the pension premium, while employees contribute the remaining 30%. A dedicated mentoring program to help you get to know the university and the Dutch (research) environment. A Development Track with the prospect of becoming an Associate Professor. If you have a more senior profile, a tailor-made career proposal will be considered. High-quality training programs for academic leadership and teaching. An excellent technical infrastructure, on-campus children's day care. Unlimited access to the modern on‑campus TU/e Student Sports Center at an exceptionally affordable rate. We support your wellbeing with free 24/7 access to OpenUp, providing you and your family with mental health support, expert guidance, and online training. Partially paid parental leave and an allowance for commuting, working from home and internet costs. A Staff Immigration Team is available for international candidates , as are a tax compensation scheme (the Expat Scheme ) and partner career support . On our website you can discover even more information about our conditions of employment . Build on your career at TU/e! About Us We are a leading international university where scientific curiosity meets a hands-on mindset. We work in an open and collaborative way with high-tech industries to tackle complex societal challenges. Our responsible and respectful approach ensures impact — today and in the future. TU/e is home to over 13,000 students and more than 7,000 staff, forming a diverse and vibrant academic community. Discover what Light Up means to TU/e in our short company video . Our university is located in Brainport Eindhoven — a world‑leading tech region with more than 7,000 high‑tech companies and strong R&D activity. Known for breakthroughs in AI, photonics, semiconductors and advanced manufacturing, Brainport is a place where technology serves people and society. Learn more about the Brainport region here . Information Do you recognize yourself in this profile and would you like to know more? Please contact the hiring manager Martin van Sint Annaland, Professor, M.v.SintAnnaland[at]tue.nl or +31 40 247 2241. Visit our website for more information about the application process . You can also contact Thomas Slegers, Senior Recruiter, t.slegers[at]tue.nl or +316 1483 5214. Curious to hear more about what it's like as a professor at TU/e? Please watch the video . Are you inspired and would like to know more about working at TU/e? Please visit our career page . Application We invite you to submit a complete application. The application should include a: Cover letter in which you describe your motivation and qualifications for the position. Curriculum vitae, including a list of your publications and the contact information of three references. Kindly note that we may reach out to references at any stage of the recruitment process. We recommend notifying your references upon submitting your application. Description of your scientific interests and plans (1-2 pages). Statement of your teaching goals and experience (1-2 pages). Ensure that you submit all the requested application documents. Please note that incomplete applications may not be considered and could be rejected. Please note You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. A pre-employment screening (e.g. knowledge security check) can be part of the selection procedure. For more information on the knowledge security check, please consult the National Knowledge Security Guidelines . Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Reference number: 2026/652 Apply now Share this vacancy Share Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Related vacancies Assistant/Associate Professor In III-V Photonic Integration Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Assistant Professor, Associate Professor Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 04-12-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 8.992 Read more Assistant/Associate Professor In High-Frequency InP Electronics Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Assistant Professor, Associate Professor Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 04-12-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 8.992 Read more Assistant/Associate Professor In Physics and engineering of reliability in PICs Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Assistant Professor, Associate Professor Organisation: Department of Electrical Engineering Apply no later than: 04-12-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 8.992 Read more Why join TU/e? Join the Eindhoven University of Technology and its thriving community of scientists, students, and professionals. Shape your own career as you become part of a personal university with a big impact. A university where students and lecturers know each other on a first-name basis and work together on innovative projects with real-life significance. Why TU/e? Excellent fundamental research combined with a hands-on mentality Explore our research State-of-the-art research labs Explore our labs World-leading university in cooperation with industry Explore our ecosystem Bachelor programs Master programs Admission and enrollment Working at TU/e Search staff Route & map Education Guide Intranet Cursor Navigation address De Zaale Eindhoven Phone number: +31 (0)40 247 9111 Contact Postal address PO Box 513 5600 MB Eindhoven Follow us Like TU/e on Facebook Follow TU/e on LinkedIn Follow TU/e on YouTube © 2026 TU/e Disclaimer Privacy Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor Education Education Education Why study at TU/e Bachelor College Graduate School Become a TU/e student Academy for Learning and Teaching TU/e innovation Space Professional Education Research Research Research Institutes Research Areas Research Groups Research Labs Research Projects Researchers Departments Grants & Awards Research Support Our university Our university Our university About the University Departments Calendar and events TU/e Campus Library Community Student Teams Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Support Staff PhD EngD At TU/e News and Events News and Events News and Events News overview Media relations Impact Impact Impact Cooperation with Industry Knowledge Transfer Office TU/e Participations Starting your business Intellectual Property Stay rates Brainport for Eachother TU/e Image Bank Educationguide Intranet Cursor"
